0
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
BLACK SCREEN

1
00:00:21,350 --> 00:00:24,630
I killed Sirius Black!

2
00:00:29,520 --> 00:00:31,060
He's back.

3
00:02:55,080 --> 00:02:57,790
The police are continuing with the investigation...

4
00:02:57,960 --> 00:03:00,000
... into the cause of the millennium bridge disaster.

5
00:03:00,170 --> 00:03:03,870
Traffic has been halted as police search for survivors.

6
00:03:04,050 --> 00:03:05,710
The surrounding area remains closed.

7
00:03:05,880 --> 00:03:09,050
The mayor has urged londoners to remain calm...

8
00:03:14,480 --> 00:03:15,640
"Harry Potter."

9
00:03:16,060 --> 00:03:17,800
Who's Harry Potter?

10
00:03:19,360 --> 00:03:21,350
Oh, no one.

11
00:03:21,900 --> 00:03:23,280
Bit of a tosser, really.

12
00:03:25,780 --> 00:03:27,440
Funny, that paper of yours.

13
00:03:27,610 --> 00:03:28,660
Couple nights ago

14
00:03:28,660 --> 00:03:30,240
I could've sworn I saw a picture move.

15
00:03:30,410 --> 00:03:33,200
- Really? - Thought I was going around the twist.

16
00:03:39,880 --> 00:03:44,500
- Hey, I was wondering... - Eleven. That's when I get off.

17
00:03:44,670 --> 00:03:47,460
You can tell me all about that tosser Harry Potter.

18
00:04:38,350 --> 00:04:40,590
You've been reckless this summer, Harry.

19
00:04:40,770 --> 00:04:43,060
I like riding around on trains.

20
00:04:44,070 --> 00:04:46,220
Takes my mind off things.

21
00:04:47,740 --> 00:04:49,650
Rather unpleasant to behold, isn't it?

22
00:04:49,820 --> 00:04:53,160
The tale is thrilling, if I say so myself.

23
00:04:53,330 --> 00:04:55,860
But now is not the time to tell it.

24
00:04:56,040 --> 00:04:57,610
Take my arm.

25
00:05:00,790 --> 00:05:02,530
Do as I say.

26
00:05:11,640 --> 00:05:13,130
I just apparated, didn't i?

27
00:05:13,300 --> 00:05:16,470
Indeed. Quite successfully too, I might add.

28
00:05:16,640 --> 00:05:19,260
Most people vomit the first time.

29
00:05:19,430 --> 00:05:21,180
I can't imagine why.

30
00:05:28,820 --> 00:05:32,650
Welcome to the charming village of Budleigh Babberton.

31
00:05:32,820 --> 00:05:37,120
Harry, I assume, right about now, you're wondering why I brought you here.

32
00:05:37,290 --> 00:05:38,990
Am I right?

33
00:05:39,160 --> 00:05:42,530
Actually, sir, after all these years, I just sort of go with it.

34
00:05:47,130 --> 00:05:48,920
Wands out, Harry.

35
00:06:00,350 --> 00:06:01,810
Horace?

36
00:06:13,950 --> 00:06:15,360
Horace?

37
00:07:07,420 --> 00:07:08,910
Merlin's beard!

38
00:07:10,090 --> 00:07:12,380
No need to disfigure me, Albus.

39
00:07:12,550 --> 00:07:16,250
Well, I must say you make a very convincing armchair, Horace.

40
00:07:17,260 --> 00:07:20,510
It's all in the upholstery. I come by the stuffing naturally.

41
00:07:20,510 --> 00:07:21,590
What gave me away?

42
00:07:22,600 --> 00:07:24,430
Dragon's blood.

43
00:07:24,850 --> 00:07:27,970
- Oh. - Oh, yes, introductions.

44
00:07:28,150 --> 00:07:32,140
Harry, I'd like you to meet an old friend and colleague of mine...

45
00:07:32,320 --> 00:07:33,780
...Horace Slughorn.

46
00:07:33,940 --> 00:07:35,440
Horace...

47
00:07:35,610 --> 00:07:38,400
...Well, you know who this is.

48
00:07:38,950 --> 00:07:41,270
Harry Potter.

49
00:07:44,120 --> 00:07:45,860
What's with all the theatrics, Horace?

50
00:07:46,040 --> 00:07:48,500
You weren't, by any chance, waiting for someone else, were you?

51
00:07:48,670 --> 00:07:51,120
Someone else? I'm sure I don't know what you mean.

52
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:55,040
The death eaters have been trying to recruit me for over a year.

53
00:07:55,220 --> 00:07:56,540
Do you know what that's like?

54
00:07:56,720 --> 00:07:58,320
You can only say no so many times,

55
00:07:58,320 --> 00:08:00,470
So I never stay anywhere more than a week.

56
00:08:00,850 --> 00:08:02,970
Muggles who own this are in the canary islands.

57
00:08:03,140 --> 00:08:08,020
Well, I think we should put it back in order for them, don't you mind?

58
00:08:42,800 --> 00:08:44,510
That was fun.

59
00:08:45,520 --> 00:08:48,520
- Do you mind if I use the loo? - No, of course.

60
00:08:49,850 --> 00:08:52,520
Don't think I don't know why you're here, Albus.

61
00:08:52,690 --> 00:08:54,390
The answer's still no.

62
00:08:54,530 --> 00:08:58,190
Absolutely and unequivocally, no.

63
00:09:06,580 --> 00:09:08,650
You're very like your father.

64
00:09:09,790 --> 00:09:11,630
Except for the eyes. you have your...

65
00:09:11,640 --> 00:09:12,660
My mother's eyes. Yeah.

66
00:09:12,840 --> 00:09:16,540
Lily. Lovely Lily. She was exceedingly bright, your mother.

67
00:09:16,710 --> 00:09:20,050
Even more impressive when one considers she was muggle-born.

68
00:09:20,220 --> 00:09:21,740
One of my best friends is muggle-born.

69
00:09:21,740 --> 00:09:22,790
Best in our year.

70
00:09:22,970 --> 00:09:25,010
Please don't think I'm prejudiced. No, no.

71
00:09:25,180 --> 00:09:28,520
Your mother was one of my absolute favorites.

72
00:09:28,520 --> 00:09:31,350
Look, there she is. Right at the front.

73
00:09:39,860 --> 00:09:42,820
All mine. Each and every one.

74
00:09:42,990 --> 00:09:45,070
Ex-students, I mean.

75
00:09:47,240 --> 00:09:51,710
You recognize Barnabas Cuffe, editor of the Daily Prophet.

76
00:09:52,580 --> 00:09:54,160
Always takes my owl

77
00:09:54,160 --> 00:09:56,530
Should I wish to register an opinion on the news of the day.

78
00:09:57,420 --> 00:10:00,380
Gwenog Jones, captain of the Holyhead Harpies.

79
00:10:00,550 --> 00:10:03,000
Free tickets whenever I want them.

80
00:10:03,260 --> 00:10:06,180
Of course, I haven't been to a match in some time.

81
00:10:07,890 --> 00:10:09,430
Ah, yes.

82
00:10:09,600 --> 00:10:11,760
Regulus Black.

83
00:10:11,940 --> 00:10:15,890
You no doubt know of his older brother Sirius. died a few weeks ago.

84
00:10:16,060 --> 00:10:18,600
I taught the whole Black family, except Sirius.

85
00:10:18,780 --> 00:10:20,980
It's a shame. Talented boy.

86
00:10:21,150 --> 00:10:23,990
I got Regulus when he came along

87
00:10:23,990 --> 00:10:26,440
Of course, but I'd have liked the set.

88
00:10:27,330 --> 00:10:28,520
Horace?

89
00:10:29,240 --> 00:10:30,790
Do you mind if I take this?

90
00:10:35,330 --> 00:10:36,800
I do love knitting patterns.

91
00:10:36,800 --> 00:10:39,000
Yes, of course. But you're not leaving?

92
00:10:39,170 --> 00:10:42,290
I think I know a lost cause when I see one.Regrettable.

93
00:10:42,470 --> 00:10:44,760
I would have considered it a personal triumph...

94
00:10:44,930 --> 00:10:47,880
...had you consented to return to Hogwarts. Oh, well.

95
00:10:48,060 --> 00:10:51,060
You're like my friend Mr. Potter here, one of a kind.

96
00:10:51,680 --> 00:10:53,390
Well, bye-bye, Horace.

97
00:10:54,440 --> 00:10:55,720
Bye.

98
00:11:06,490 --> 00:11:09,240
All right. I'll do it.

99
00:11:09,410 --> 00:11:11,980
But I want professor Merrythought's old office,

100
00:11:11,980 --> 00:11:13,990
Not the water closet I had before.

101
00:11:14,160 --> 00:11:18,380
And I expect a raise. These are mad times we live in. mad!

102
00:11:20,170 --> 00:11:21,800
They are indeed.

103
00:11:25,220 --> 00:11:27,090
Sir, exactly what was all that about?

104
00:11:27,680 --> 00:11:30,730
You are talented, famous and powerful.

105
00:11:30,730 --> 00:11:32,340
Everything Horace values.

106
00:11:32,520 --> 00:11:35,930
Professor Slughorn is gonna try to collect you, Harry.

107
00:11:36,100 --> 00:11:38,480
You would be his crowning jewel.

108
00:11:38,650 --> 00:11:41,970
That's why he's returning to Hogwarts.

109
00:11:41,970 --> 00:11:44,190
And it's crucial he should return.

110
00:11:44,900 --> 00:11:48,020
I fear I may have stolen a wondrous night from you, Harry.

111
00:11:48,200 --> 00:11:53,240
She was, truthfully, very pretty, the girl.

112
00:11:53,410 --> 00:11:56,860
It's all right, sir. I'll go back tomorrow, make some excuse.

113
00:11:57,040 --> 00:12:00,710
Oh, you'll not be returning to Little Whinging tonight, Harry.

114
00:12:00,880 --> 00:12:03,880
But, sir, what about Hedwig? And my trunk?

115
00:12:04,050 --> 00:12:06,720
Both are waiting for you.

116
00:12:40,210 --> 00:12:41,750
Hedwig.

117
00:12:44,340 --> 00:12:45,580
Mum?

118
00:12:46,970 --> 00:12:48,340
Ginny, what is it?

119
00:12:48,760 --> 00:12:51,000
I was only wondering when Harry got here.

120
00:12:51,180 --> 00:12:53,210
What? Harry? Harry who?

121
00:12:53,210 --> 00:12:54,430
Harry Potter, of course.

122
00:12:54,600 --> 00:12:57,770
I think I'd know if Harry Potter was in my house, wouldn't i?

123
00:12:57,940 --> 00:12:59,770
His trunk's in the kitchen, and his owl.

124
00:12:59,770 --> 00:13:01,430
No, dear, I seriously doubt that.

125
00:13:04,070 --> 00:13:05,730
Harry? Did someone say "Harry"?

126
00:13:05,900 --> 00:13:07,860
Me, nosy. Is he up there with you?

127
00:13:08,030 --> 00:13:08,880
Of course not.

128
00:13:08,880 --> 00:13:11,060
I'd know if my best friend was in my room, wouldn't i?

129
00:13:11,240 --> 00:13:13,730
- Is that an owl? - You haven't seen him, have you?

130
00:13:13,910 --> 00:13:15,650
Apparently he's wandering about the house.

131
00:13:15,830 --> 00:13:17,570
- Really? - Really.

132
00:13:17,830 --> 00:13:19,410
Harry!

133
00:13:25,630 --> 00:13:27,340
Harry!

134
00:13:29,260 --> 00:13:32,540
What a lovely surprise.

135
00:13:34,640 --> 00:13:36,960
Why didn't you let us know you were coming?

136
00:13:37,140 --> 00:13:39,360
I didn't know. Dumbledore.

137
00:13:39,360 --> 00:13:39,980
Oh, that man.

138
00:13:40,140 --> 00:13:42,390
But then, what would we do without him?

139
00:13:43,650 --> 00:13:46,320
Got a bit of toothpaste.

140
00:13:53,530 --> 00:13:54,940
So when did you get here?

141
00:13:55,120 --> 00:13:56,830
A few days ago.

142
00:13:57,740 --> 00:14:00,070
Though for a while, I wasn't sure I was coming.

143
00:14:01,870 --> 00:14:04,160
Mum sort of lost it last week.

144
00:14:04,460 --> 00:14:07,300
Said Ginny and I had no business going back to Hogwarts.

145
00:14:07,460 --> 00:14:08,840
That it's too dangerous.

146
00:14:09,010 --> 00:14:11,840
- Oh, come on. - She's not alone.

147
00:14:12,010 --> 00:14:15,340
Even my parents, and they're muggles, know something bad's happening.

148
00:14:15,510 --> 00:14:19,380
Anyway, dad stepped in, told her she was being barmy...

149
00:14:19,680 --> 00:14:22,090
...and it took a few days, but she came around.

150
00:14:23,440 --> 00:14:25,490
But this is Hogwarts we're talking about.

151
00:14:25,490 --> 00:14:26,260
It's Dumbledore.

152
00:14:26,260 --> 00:14:27,350
What could be safer?

153
00:14:28,030 --> 00:14:31,230
There's been a lot of talk recently that...

154
00:14:31,990 --> 00:14:33,700
...Dumbledore's got a bit old.

155
00:14:33,860 --> 00:14:35,660
Rubbish! well, he's only...

156
00:14:35,820 --> 00:14:37,400
What is he?

157
00:14:37,580 --> 00:14:40,780
Hundred and fifty? Give or take a few years.

158
00:15:00,850 --> 00:15:04,680
Cissy! You can't do this! He can't be trusted!

159
00:15:04,850 --> 00:15:06,310
The dark lord trusts him.

160
00:15:06,480 --> 00:15:10,060
The dark lord's mistaken.

161
00:15:39,350 --> 00:15:41,590
Run along, Wormtail.

162
00:15:44,480 --> 00:15:47,100
I know I ought not to be here.

163
00:15:48,230 --> 00:15:50,980
The dark lord himself forbade me to speak of this.

164
00:15:51,150 --> 00:15:53,820
If the dark lord has forbidden it, you ought not to speak.

165
00:15:53,990 --> 00:15:58,230
Put it down, Bella. We mustn't touch what isn't ours.

166
00:16:02,370 --> 00:16:06,070
As it so happens, I'm aware of your situation, Narcissa.

167
00:16:06,250 --> 00:16:07,410
You?

168
00:16:08,500 --> 00:16:10,790
The dark lord told you?

169
00:16:11,380 --> 00:16:13,920
Your sister doubts me.

170
00:16:14,970 --> 00:16:17,800
Understandable. Over the years I've played my part well.

171
00:16:17,970 --> 00:16:21,720
So well, I've deceived one of the greatest wizards of all time.

172
00:16:23,140 --> 00:16:27,050
Dumbledore is a great wizard. Only a fool would question it.

173
00:16:27,230 --> 00:16:29,140
I don't doubt you, Severus.

174
00:16:29,310 --> 00:16:32,480
You should be honored, Cissy. As should Draco.

175
00:16:36,900 --> 00:16:38,780
He's just a boy.

176
00:16:39,660 --> 00:16:42,660
I can't change the dark lord's mind.

177
00:16:44,290 --> 00:16:47,950
But it might be possible for me to help Draco.

178
00:16:49,710 --> 00:16:52,630
- Severus. - Swear to it.

179
00:16:56,720 --> 00:16:59,120
Make the unbreakable vow.

180
00:17:03,010 --> 00:17:06,050
It's just empty words.

181
00:17:06,230 --> 00:17:09,430
He'll give it his best effort.

182
00:17:09,600 --> 00:17:11,980
But when it matters most...

183
00:17:13,770 --> 00:17:17,820
...he'll just slither back into his hole.

184
00:17:21,280 --> 00:17:22,910
Coward.

185
00:17:25,950 --> 00:17:29,540
Take out your wand.

186
00:17:42,720 --> 00:17:43,880
Will you...

187
00:17:44,050 --> 00:17:46,090
...Severus Snape...

188
00:17:46,270 --> 00:17:49,180
...watch over Draco Malfoy...

189
00:17:49,350 --> 00:17:54,180
...as he attempts to fulfill the dark lord's wishes?

190
00:17:55,320 --> 00:17:57,230
I will.

191
00:17:58,610 --> 00:18:02,280
And will you, to the best of your ability...

192
00:18:02,950 --> 00:18:05,150
...protect him from harm?

193
00:18:06,620 --> 00:18:07,900
I will.

194
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:12,490
And if Draco should fail...

195
00:18:13,630 --> 00:18:18,250
...will you yourself carry out the deed...

196
00:18:18,420 --> 00:18:23,420
...the dark lord has ordered Draco to perform?

197
00:18:28,680 --> 00:18:30,180
I will.

198
00:18:52,960 --> 00:18:55,960
Step up! Step up! We've got fainting fancies!

199
00:18:56,130 --> 00:18:57,160
Nosebleed nougats!

200
00:18:57,340 --> 00:19:00,420
- And just in time for school... - Puking pastilles!

201
00:19:02,210 --> 00:19:04,210
- Into the cauldRon, handsome. - Into the cauldRon, handsome.

202
00:19:06,820 --> 00:19:07,710
I will have order!

203
00:19:07,890 --> 00:19:12,270
I really hate children. I will have order!

204
00:19:18,400 --> 00:19:21,320
- Peruvian instant darkness powder. - A real money spinner, that.

205
00:19:21,490 --> 00:19:23,610
Handy if you need to make a quick getaway.

206
00:19:23,780 --> 00:19:25,520
- Hello, ladies. - Hello, ladies.

207
00:19:25,700 --> 00:19:28,980
- Love potions, eh? - Yeah, they really do work.

208
00:19:29,160 --> 00:19:31,220
Then again, the way we hear it, sis

209
00:19:31,220 --> 00:19:32,490
You're doing just fine on your own.

210
00:19:32,660 --> 00:19:33,830
Meaning?

211
00:19:34,000 --> 00:19:36,120
Are you not currently dating Dean Thomas?

212
00:19:36,580 --> 00:19:38,330
It's none of your business.

213
00:19:44,090 --> 00:19:45,120
How much for this?

214
00:19:45,300 --> 00:19:46,680
- Five galleons. - Five galleons.

215
00:19:46,840 --> 00:19:48,970
- How much for me? - Five galleons.

216
00:19:49,140 --> 00:19:50,340
I'm your brother.

217
00:19:50,720 --> 00:19:52,760
- Ten galleons. - Ten galleons.

218
00:19:54,690 --> 00:19:56,350
Come on, let's go.

219
00:19:58,810 --> 00:20:00,230
Hi, Ron.

220
00:20:00,940 --> 00:20:02,270
Hi.

221
00:20:15,500 --> 00:20:18,190
How are Fred and George doing it?

222
00:20:18,200 --> 00:20:19,540
Half the alley's closed down.

223
00:20:19,710 --> 00:20:22,280
Fred reckons people need a laugh these days.

224
00:20:22,750 --> 00:20:24,710
I reckon he's right.

225
00:20:26,510 --> 00:20:28,090
Oh, no.

226
00:20:28,720 --> 00:20:30,880
Everyone got their wands from ollivander's.

227
00:20:43,360 --> 00:20:44,730
Harry?

228
00:20:46,570 --> 00:20:48,650
Is it me, or do Draco and mummy look like two people...

229
00:20:48,820 --> 00:20:50,530
...who don't want to be followed?

230
00:22:35,760 --> 00:22:37,090
Quibbler.

231
00:22:38,890 --> 00:22:40,430
Quibbler.

232
00:22:42,350 --> 00:22:47,010
He's lovely. They've been known to sing on boxing day, you know.

233
00:22:47,190 --> 00:22:49,560
- Quibbler? - Oh, please.

234
00:22:50,780 --> 00:22:53,320
- What's a wrackspurt? - They're invisible creatures.

235
00:22:53,490 --> 00:22:56,660
They float in your ears and make your brain go fuzzy.

236
00:22:57,200 --> 00:22:58,740
Quibbler.

237
00:23:09,210 --> 00:23:11,960
So, what was Draco doing with that weird-looking cabinet?

238
00:23:12,130 --> 00:23:13,840
And who were all those people?

239
00:23:14,010 --> 00:23:17,130
Don't you see? It was a ceremony, an initiation.

240
00:23:17,300 --> 00:23:19,210
Stop it, Harry. I know where you're going.

241
00:23:19,390 --> 00:23:21,880
It's happened. He's one of them.

242
00:23:22,060 --> 00:23:23,550
One of what?

243
00:23:24,310 --> 00:23:27,760
Harry is under the impression Draco Malfoy is now a death eater.

244
00:23:27,940 --> 00:23:29,900
You're barking.

245
00:23:30,070 --> 00:23:32,190
What would you-know-who want with Malfoy?

246
00:23:32,360 --> 00:23:36,410
Well, then what's he doing in borgin and burkes? Browsing for furniture?

247
00:23:36,570 --> 00:23:38,450
It's a creepy shop. He's a creepy bloke.

248
00:23:38,620 --> 00:23:42,480
Look, his father is a death eater. It only makes sense.

249
00:23:42,660 --> 00:23:44,240
Hermione saw it with her own eyes.

250
00:23:44,410 --> 00:23:47,750
I told you, I don't know what I saw.

251
00:23:49,460 --> 00:23:51,000
I need some air.

252
00:24:07,730 --> 00:24:11,510
Don't worry. When we get to Hogwarts, we'll sort it out.

253
00:24:31,920 --> 00:24:35,170
- What was that? Blaise? - Don't know.

254
00:24:35,340 --> 00:24:38,460
Relax, boys. It's probably just a first-year messing around.

255
00:24:38,640 --> 00:24:42,000
Come on, Draco. Sit down. We'll be at Hogwarts soon.

256
00:24:51,690 --> 00:24:55,470
Hogwarts. What a pathetic excuse for a school.

257
00:24:55,650 --> 00:24:57,650
I'd pitch myself off the astronomy tower...

258
00:24:57,820 --> 00:24:59,940
...if I had to continue for another two years.

259
00:25:00,120 --> 00:25:01,440
What's that supposed to mean?

260
00:25:02,700 --> 00:25:06,530
Let's just say you won't see me wasting my time in charms class next year.

261
00:25:08,330 --> 00:25:10,160
Amused, Blaise?

262
00:25:11,630 --> 00:25:14,030
We'll see just who's laughing in the end.

263
00:25:36,190 --> 00:25:39,940
You two go on. I wanna check something.

264
00:25:42,120 --> 00:25:43,400
Where's Harry?

265
00:25:43,580 --> 00:25:46,530
He's probably already on the platform. Come on.

266
00:26:02,220 --> 00:26:05,720
Didn't mummy ever tell you it was rude to eavesdrop, Potter?

267
00:26:05,890 --> 00:26:07,470
Petrificus totalus.

268
00:26:18,690 --> 00:26:20,150
Oh, yeah...

269
00:26:20,570 --> 00:26:23,860
...she was dead before you could wipe the drool off your chin.

270
00:26:29,370 --> 00:26:32,540
That's for my father. Enjoy your ride back to london.

271
00:27:16,380 --> 00:27:18,120
Finite.

272
00:27:24,260 --> 00:27:25,540
- Hello, Harry. - Luna!

273
00:27:25,930 --> 00:27:28,500
How'd you know where I was?

274
00:27:28,500 --> 00:27:30,640
Wrackspurts. Your head's full of them.

275
00:27:37,360 --> 00:27:40,030
Sorry I made you miss the carriages, by the way, Luna.

276
00:27:40,190 --> 00:27:43,360
That's all right. It was like being with a friend.

277
00:27:43,530 --> 00:27:45,570
Oh, I am your friend, Luna.

278
00:27:45,990 --> 00:27:47,780
That's nice.

279
00:27:47,950 --> 00:27:51,150
About time. I've been looking all over for you two.

280
00:27:51,330 --> 00:27:54,160
Right. Names?

281
00:27:54,410 --> 00:27:56,790
Professor Flitwick, you've known me for five years.

282
00:27:56,960 --> 00:27:59,080
No exceptions, Potter.

283
00:27:59,630 --> 00:28:01,370
Who are those people?

284
00:28:01,550 --> 00:28:03,840
Aurors. For security.

285
00:28:04,010 --> 00:28:05,470
What's this cane here, then?

286
00:28:05,760 --> 00:28:08,000
It's not a cane, you cretin. It's a walking stick.

287
00:28:08,180 --> 00:28:12,180
And what exactly would you be wanting with a...?

288
00:28:13,350 --> 00:28:16,430
Could be construed as an offensive weapon.

289
00:28:16,600 --> 00:28:21,850
It's all right, Mr. Filch. I can vouch for Mr. Malfoy.

290
00:28:29,240 --> 00:28:31,200
Nice face, Potter.

291
00:28:37,750 --> 00:28:40,080
Would you like me to fix it for you?

292
00:28:40,250 --> 00:28:44,040
Personally, I think you look a bit more devil-may-care this way...

293
00:28:44,210 --> 00:28:45,760
...But it's up to you.

294
00:28:46,180 --> 00:28:48,460
Well, have you ever fixed a nose before?

295
00:28:48,640 --> 00:28:52,340
No, but I've done several toes, and how different are they, really?

296
00:28:53,390 --> 00:28:57,300
Um... okay, yeah. Give it a go.

297
00:28:59,730 --> 00:29:01,770
Episkey.

298
00:29:07,910 --> 00:29:11,070
- How do I look? - Exceptionally ordinary.

299
00:29:12,200 --> 00:29:13,580
Brilliant.

300
00:29:20,960 --> 00:29:23,000
Don't worry. He'll be here in a minute.

301
00:29:26,880 --> 00:29:29,590
Will you stop eating?

302
00:29:29,760 --> 00:29:32,000
Your best friend is missing!

303
00:29:32,180 --> 00:29:35,430
Oi. Turn around, you lunatic.

304
00:29:38,230 --> 00:29:39,720
He's covered in blood again.

305
00:29:40,350 --> 00:29:42,290
Why is it he's always covered in blood?

306
00:29:42,290 --> 00:29:44,140
Looks like it's his own this time.

307
00:29:44,610 --> 00:29:46,480
Where have you been?

308
00:29:46,650 --> 00:29:49,110
- What happened to your face? - Later.

309
00:29:49,280 --> 00:29:50,900
What've I missed?

310
00:29:51,450 --> 00:29:55,230
Sorting hat urged us all to be brave and strong in these troubled times.

311
00:29:55,410 --> 00:29:58,950
Easy for it to say, huh? It's a hat, isn't it?

312
00:30:06,800 --> 00:30:08,510
Very best of evenings to you all.

313
00:30:08,670 --> 00:30:09,710
Thanks.

314
00:30:11,930 --> 00:30:16,590
First off, let me introduce the newest member of our staff...

315
00:30:16,770 --> 00:30:19,010
...Horace Slughorn.

316
00:30:22,900 --> 00:30:24,770
Professor Slughorn, I'm happy to say...

317
00:30:24,940 --> 00:30:29,230
...has agreed to resume his old post as potions master.

318
00:30:29,400 --> 00:30:32,320
Meanwhile, the post of defense against the dark arts...

319
00:30:32,490 --> 00:30:34,280
...will be taken by professor Snape.

320
00:30:34,700 --> 00:30:36,160
Snape?

321
00:30:42,210 --> 00:30:43,830
Now, as you know...

322
00:30:44,000 --> 00:30:47,670
...each and every one of you was searched upon your arrival here tonight.

323
00:30:47,840 --> 00:30:49,830
And you have the right to know why.

324
00:30:50,630 --> 00:30:54,220
Once there was a young man, who, like you...

325
00:30:54,390 --> 00:30:56,840
...Sat in this very hall...

326
00:30:57,220 --> 00:31:01,850
...Walked this castle's corridors, slept under its roof.

327
00:31:02,440 --> 00:31:06,810
He seemed to all the world a student like any other.

328
00:31:06,980 --> 00:31:08,520
His name?

329
00:31:09,990 --> 00:31:11,310
Tom Riddle.

330
00:31:16,490 --> 00:31:18,150
Today, of course...

331
00:31:18,700 --> 00:31:22,040
...He's known all over the world by another name.

332
00:31:23,210 --> 00:31:28,410
Which is why, as I stand looking out upon you all tonight...

333
00:31:28,590 --> 00:31:30,960
...I'm reminded of a sobering fact.

334
00:31:32,130 --> 00:31:35,250
Every day, every hour...

335
00:31:35,430 --> 00:31:37,380
...This very minute, perhaps...

336
00:31:37,550 --> 00:31:41,880
...Dark forces attempt to penetrate this castle's walls.

337
00:31:43,520 --> 00:31:49,060
But in the end, their greatest weapon is you.

338
00:31:52,110 --> 00:31:54,230
Just something to think about.

339
00:31:55,490 --> 00:31:57,070
Now, off to bed. Pip-pip.

340
00:31:58,740 --> 00:32:00,530
That was cheerful.

341
00:32:05,830 --> 00:32:10,580
History of magic is upstairs, ladies, not down.

342
00:32:11,380 --> 00:32:16,370
Mr. davies! Mr. davies! That is the girls' lavatory.

343
00:32:19,180 --> 00:32:20,590
Potter.

344
00:32:21,930 --> 00:32:23,890
Oh, this can't be good.

345
00:32:27,190 --> 00:32:28,560
Enjoying ourselves, are we?

346
00:32:29,480 --> 00:32:32,680
- I had a free period this morning. - So I noticed.

347
00:32:33,190 --> 00:32:35,600
I would think you would want to fill it with potions.

348
00:32:35,780 --> 00:32:38,450
Or is it no longer your ambition to become an auror?

349
00:32:39,240 --> 00:32:42,860
It was, but I was told I had to get an "Outstanding" in my O.W.L.

350
00:32:43,040 --> 00:32:45,910
So you did, when professor Snape was teaching potions.

351
00:32:46,080 --> 00:32:49,790
However, professor Slughorn is perfectly happy to accept N.E.W.T.

352
00:32:49,790 --> 00:32:50,660
S students...

353
00:32:50,840 --> 00:32:52,630
...with "Exceeds expectations."

354
00:32:53,130 --> 00:32:54,790
Brilliant. Um...

355
00:32:54,970 --> 00:32:57,420
- Well, I'll head there straightaway. - Oh, good, good.

356
00:32:57,590 --> 00:33:02,500
Potter, take Weasley with you. He looks far too happy over there.

357
00:33:04,310 --> 00:33:05,590
I don't wanna take potions.

358
00:33:05,770 --> 00:33:08,470
This is quidditch trials coming up. I need to practice.

359
00:33:09,730 --> 00:33:11,690
Attention to detail in the preparation...

360
00:33:11,860 --> 00:33:14,150
...Is the prerequisite of all planning.

361
00:33:17,200 --> 00:33:19,150
Harry, my boy, I was beginning to worry.

362
00:33:19,150 --> 00:33:21,110
We've brought someone with us, I see.

363
00:33:21,740 --> 00:33:22,940
Ron Weasley, Sir.

364
00:33:23,490 --> 00:33:25,950
But I'm dead awful at potions, a menace, actually.

365
00:33:26,120 --> 00:33:28,200
- I'm gonna... - Nonsense, we'll sort you out.

366
00:33:28,370 --> 00:33:31,460
Any friend of Harry's is a friend of mine. Get your books out.

367
00:33:31,630 --> 00:33:34,170
I haven't actually got my book yet, and nor has Ron.

368
00:33:34,340 --> 00:33:36,050
Get what you want from the cupboard.

369
00:33:36,220 --> 00:33:39,550
Now, as I was saying, I prepared some concoctions this morning.

370
00:33:39,720 --> 00:33:43,670
Any ideas what these might be?

371
00:33:45,180 --> 00:33:47,760
-Yes, Miss...? - Granger, sir.

372
00:33:51,020 --> 00:33:55,480
That one there is veritaserum. It's a truth-telling serum.

373
00:33:55,650 --> 00:33:58,360
And that would be polyjuice potion.

374
00:34:01,990 --> 00:34:03,650
It's terribly tricky to make.

375
00:34:03,830 --> 00:34:05,870
And this is amortentia...

376
00:34:06,040 --> 00:34:08,440
...The most powerful love potion in the world.

377
00:34:09,370 --> 00:34:11,080
It's rumored to smell differently to

378
00:34:11,080 --> 00:34:13,210
Each person according to what attracts them.

379
00:34:14,500 --> 00:34:16,500
For example, I smell...

380
00:34:17,260 --> 00:34:21,300
...Freshly mown grass, and new parchment, and...

381
00:34:21,470 --> 00:34:24,800
...Spearmint toothpaste.

382
00:34:26,220 --> 00:34:29,670
Amortentia doesn't create actual love. That would be impossible.

383
00:34:29,850 --> 00:34:34,850
But it does cause a powerful infatuation or obsession.

384
00:34:35,020 --> 00:34:36,710
And for that reason,

385
00:34:36,710 --> 00:34:41,690
It is probably the most dangerous potion in this room.

386
00:34:47,240 --> 00:34:50,030
Sir? You haven't told us what's in that one.

387
00:34:50,410 --> 00:34:52,120
Oh, yes.

388
00:34:52,290 --> 00:34:54,860
What you see before you, ladies and gentlemen...

389
00:34:55,040 --> 00:35:00,460
...is a curious little potion known as felix felicis.

390
00:35:00,880 --> 00:35:03,120
But it is more commonly referred to as...

391
00:35:03,300 --> 00:35:08,590
- Liquid luck. - Yes, Miss Granger. Liquid luck.

392
00:35:09,100 --> 00:35:12,100
Desperately tricky to make, disastrous should you get it wrong.

393
00:35:12,900 --> 00:35:17,890
One sip and you will find that all of your endeavors succeed.

394
00:35:19,940 --> 00:35:22,430
At least until the effects wear off.

395
00:35:23,280 --> 00:35:27,110
So this is what I offer each of you today.

396
00:35:27,280 --> 00:35:31,920
One tiny vial of liquid luck to the student who, in the hour that remains.

397
00:35:32,290 --> 00:35:36,870
...Manages to brew an acceptable draught of living death...

398
00:35:37,040 --> 00:35:40,290
...The recipes for which can be found on page 10 of your books.

399
00:35:40,460 --> 00:35:41,720
I should point out, however,

400
00:35:41,720 --> 00:35:44,130
Only once did a student manage to brew a potion...

401
00:35:44,300 --> 00:35:47,640
...Of sufficient quality to claim this prize.

402
00:35:48,310 --> 00:35:50,460
Nevertheless, good luck to you all.

403
00:35:51,350 --> 00:35:53,140
Let the brewing commence.

404
00:36:28,970 --> 00:36:30,800
How did you do that?

405
00:36:31,350 --> 00:36:33,510
You crush it. Don't cut it.

406
00:36:33,680 --> 00:36:36,180
No. The instructions specifically say to cut.

407
00:36:36,350 --> 00:36:38,180
No, really.

408
00:37:15,680 --> 00:37:18,850
Merlin's beard! It is perfect.

409
00:37:20,360 --> 00:37:23,560
So perfect I daresay one drop would kill us all.

410
00:37:26,860 --> 00:37:28,820
So here we are, then, as promised.

411
00:37:28,990 --> 00:37:32,190
One vial of felix felicis.

412
00:37:32,370 --> 00:37:34,410
Congratulations.

413
00:37:34,910 --> 00:37:37,660
Use it well.

414
00:38:05,280 --> 00:38:07,950
Harry, you got my message. Come in.

415
00:38:09,610 --> 00:38:10,990
How are you?

416
00:38:11,160 --> 00:38:12,700
I'm fine, sir.

417
00:38:12,870 --> 00:38:14,110
Enjoying your classes?

418
00:38:15,370 --> 00:38:18,410
I know professor Slughorn is most impressed with you.

419
00:38:19,120 --> 00:38:21,410
I think he overestimates my abilities, sir.

420
00:38:22,130 --> 00:38:23,240
Do you?

421
00:38:23,790 --> 00:38:25,040
Definitely.

422
00:38:27,050 --> 00:38:29,880
What about your activities outside the classroom?

423
00:38:31,090 --> 00:38:33,090
- Sir? - Well, I notice you spend...

424
00:38:33,260 --> 00:38:35,880
...A great deal of time with Miss Granger.

425
00:38:36,060 --> 00:38:37,300
I can't help wondering...

426
00:38:37,470 --> 00:38:42,470
Oh, no, no. I mean, she's brilliant, and we're friends, but, no.

427
00:38:42,650 --> 00:38:45,650
Forgive me. I was merely being curious.

428
00:38:46,730 --> 00:38:48,610
But enough chitchat.

429
00:38:48,820 --> 00:38:52,400
You must be wondering why I summoned you here tonight.

430
00:38:52,990 --> 00:38:55,830
The answer lies here.

431
00:38:56,830 --> 00:38:58,990
What you are looking at are memories.

432
00:38:59,160 --> 00:39:02,990
In this case, pertaining to one individual, Voldemort...

433
00:39:03,170 --> 00:39:05,620
...Or, as he was known then, Tom Riddle.

434
00:39:08,670 --> 00:39:12,500
This vial contains the most particular memory...

435
00:39:12,680 --> 00:39:14,880
...Of the day I first met him.

436
00:39:16,220 --> 00:39:19,010
I'd like you to see it, if you would.

437
00:39:56,640 --> 00:40:00,880
I admit some confusion upon receiving your letter, Mr. Dumbledore.

438
00:40:01,230 --> 00:40:04,680
In all the years Tom's been here, he's never once had a family visitor.

439
00:40:04,850 --> 00:40:08,600
There have been incidents with the other children. Nasty things.

440
00:40:11,030 --> 00:40:13,180
Tom, you have a visitor.

441
00:40:13,740 --> 00:40:15,400
How do you do, Tom?

442
00:40:22,910 --> 00:40:24,160
Don't.

443
00:40:31,960 --> 00:40:35,080
- You're the doctor, aren't you? - No.

444
00:40:35,260 --> 00:40:37,300
I am a professor.

445
00:40:38,010 --> 00:40:39,840
I don't believe you.

446
00:40:40,010 --> 00:40:42,010
She wants me looked at.

447
00:40:42,600 --> 00:40:44,810
They think I'm different.

448
00:40:44,980 --> 00:40:46,470
Well, perhaps they're right.

449
00:40:46,650 --> 00:40:48,100
I'm not mad.

450
00:40:48,270 --> 00:40:51,610
Hogwarts is not a place for mad people.

451
00:40:51,780 --> 00:40:53,770
Hogwarts is a school.

452
00:40:54,530 --> 00:40:55,690
A school of magic.

453
00:41:00,200 --> 00:41:02,950
You can do things, can't you, Tom?

454
00:41:04,080 --> 00:41:06,750
Things other children can't.

455
00:41:08,130 --> 00:41:11,080
I can make things move without touching them.

456
00:41:12,000 --> 00:41:15,590
I can make animals do what I want without training them.

457
00:41:16,380 --> 00:41:19,920
I can make bad things happen to people who are mean to me.

458
00:41:20,550 --> 00:41:22,510
I can make them hurt...

459
00:41:23,140 --> 00:41:24,680
...If I want.

460
00:41:25,230 --> 00:41:27,100
Who are you?

461
00:41:27,270 --> 00:41:29,480
Well, I'm like you, Tom.

462
00:41:30,650 --> 00:41:32,110
I'm different.

463
00:41:33,150 --> 00:41:34,560
Prove it.

464
00:41:42,160 --> 00:41:45,990
I think there's something in your wardrobe trying to get out, Tom.

465
00:41:55,710 --> 00:41:59,500
Thievery is not tolerated at Hogwarts, Tom.

466
00:41:59,680 --> 00:42:03,620
At Hogwarts, you'll be taught not only how to use magic,

467
00:42:03,620 --> 00:42:05,350
But how to control it.

468
00:42:05,520 --> 00:42:06,680
You understand me?

469
00:42:10,650 --> 00:42:13,180
I can speak to snakes too.

470
00:42:14,440 --> 00:42:16,230
They find me.

471
00:42:17,240 --> 00:42:19,150
Whisper things.

472
00:42:19,400 --> 00:42:22,520
Is that normal for someone like me?

473
00:42:43,600 --> 00:42:46,880
Did you know, sir? Then?

474
00:42:47,060 --> 00:42:52,680
Did I know I'd just met the most dangerous dark wizard of all time? No.

475
00:42:53,270 --> 00:42:55,400
If I had, I...

476
00:42:57,030 --> 00:42:59,480
Over time, while here at Hogwarts...

477
00:42:59,650 --> 00:43:02,990
...Tom Riddle grew close to one particular teacher.

478
00:43:03,160 --> 00:43:04,980
Can you guess who that teacher might be?

479
00:43:07,910 --> 00:43:11,360
You didn't bring professor Slughorn back simply to teach potions, did you?

480
00:43:11,540 --> 00:43:13,580
No, I did not.

481
00:43:13,750 --> 00:43:17,580
You see, professor Slughorn possesses something I desire very dearly.

482
00:43:18,590 --> 00:43:20,460
And he will not give it up easily.

483
00:43:20,630 --> 00:43:23,840
You said professor Slughorn would try to collect me.

484
00:43:24,010 --> 00:43:25,260
I did.

485
00:43:25,970 --> 00:43:27,960
Do you want me to let him?

486
00:43:29,350 --> 00:43:30,730
Yes.

487
00:44:54,890 --> 00:44:56,600
All right. Um...

488
00:44:56,770 --> 00:44:59,850
This morning, I'm gonna be putting you all through a few drills...

489
00:45:00,020 --> 00:45:02,150
...just to assess your strengths.

490
00:45:02,860 --> 00:45:04,850
Quiet! Please!

491
00:45:05,030 --> 00:45:06,190
Shut it!

492
00:45:10,030 --> 00:45:12,790
Thanks. All right. Um...

493
00:45:12,950 --> 00:45:15,080
Just because you made the team last year...

494
00:45:15,250 --> 00:45:18,200
...Does not guarantee you a spot this year. Is that clear?

495
00:45:20,710 --> 00:45:21,990
Good.

496
00:45:30,720 --> 00:45:32,930
No hard feelings, Weasley, all right?

497
00:45:33,470 --> 00:45:34,670
Hard feelings?

498
00:45:34,850 --> 00:45:38,390
Yeah, I'll be going out for keeper as well. It's nothing personal.

499
00:45:38,560 --> 00:45:41,230
Really? Strapping guy like you?

500
00:45:41,400 --> 00:45:43,970
You've got more of a beater's build, don't you think?

501
00:45:44,150 --> 00:45:46,560
Keepers need to be quick, agile.

502
00:45:47,950 --> 00:45:49,740
Oh, I like my chances.

503
00:45:49,910 --> 00:45:53,690
Say, think you could introduce me to your friend Granger?

504
00:45:53,870 --> 00:45:58,030
Wouldn't mind getting on a first-name basis, know what I mean?

505
00:46:10,340 --> 00:46:12,050
Come on, Weasley!

506
00:46:12,220 --> 00:46:13,930
- Come on, Ron! - Go on, Weasley!

507
00:46:15,470 --> 00:46:18,340
- Go on, Weasley! - Yeah, Ron!

508
00:46:18,520 --> 00:46:19,760
Go on, Cormac!

509
00:46:36,290 --> 00:46:38,360
Come on, Ron!

510
00:46:46,670 --> 00:46:48,300
Come on, Ron.

511
00:46:49,050 --> 00:46:50,920
Come on, Ron.

512
00:47:08,820 --> 00:47:09,980
Confundus.

513
00:47:26,090 --> 00:47:28,410
Isn't he brilliant?

514
00:47:31,180 --> 00:47:34,670
I have to admit, I thought I was gonna miss that last one.

515
00:47:35,010 --> 00:47:37,800
I hope Cormac's not taking it too hard.

516
00:47:38,220 --> 00:47:41,260
He's got a bit of a thing for you, Hermione. Cormac.

517
00:47:42,350 --> 00:47:44,350
He's vile.

518
00:47:49,320 --> 00:47:51,560
Have you ever heard of this spell? Sectumsempra?

519
00:47:51,740 --> 00:47:53,810
No, I haven't.

520
00:47:53,990 --> 00:47:57,110
And if you had a shred of self-respect, you'd hand that book in.

521
00:47:57,280 --> 00:47:59,740
Not bloody likely. He's top of the class.

522
00:47:59,910 --> 00:48:04,080
He's even better than you, Hermione. Slughorn thinks he's a genius.

523
00:48:05,210 --> 00:48:06,490
What?

524
00:48:07,340 --> 00:48:10,040
I'd like to know whose that book was. Let's have a look.

525
00:48:10,210 --> 00:48:11,710
No.

526
00:48:13,220 --> 00:48:14,500
Why not?

527
00:48:15,050 --> 00:48:16,680
The binding is fragile.

528
00:48:16,850 --> 00:48:19,470
- The binding is fragile? - Yeah.

529
00:48:23,730 --> 00:48:25,310
- Who's the half-blood prince? - Who?

530
00:48:25,420 --> 00:48:26,340
That is said right here.

531
00:48:26,850 --> 00:48:29,230
"This book is property of the half-blood prince."

532
00:48:46,580 --> 00:48:49,920
For weeks you carry around this book, practically sleep with it...

533
00:48:50,090 --> 00:48:52,380
... Yet you have no desire to find out who the half-blood prince is?

534
00:48:52,550 --> 00:48:55,960
I didn't say I wasn't curious, and I don't sleep with it.

535
00:48:56,130 --> 00:48:57,170
Well, it's true.

536
00:48:57,340 --> 00:48:59,100
I like a nice chat before I go to bed.

537
00:48:59,100 --> 00:49:01,090
Now all you do is read that bloody book.

538
00:49:01,270 --> 00:49:03,260
It's just like being with Hermione.

539
00:49:04,560 --> 00:49:07,050
Well, I was curious, so I went to...

540
00:49:07,230 --> 00:49:09,770
- The library. - The library. And?

541
00:49:10,690 --> 00:49:12,320
And nothing.

542
00:49:12,480 --> 00:49:15,520
I couldn't find a reference anywhere to a half-blood prince.

543
00:49:15,700 --> 00:49:17,770
- There we go. That settles it, then. - Filius!

544
00:49:17,950 --> 00:49:20,270
I was hoping to find you in the three broomsticks!

545
00:49:20,450 --> 00:49:25,110
No, emergency choir practice, I'm afraid, Horace.

546
00:49:28,630 --> 00:49:31,030
Does anyone fancy a butterbeer?

547
00:49:31,380 --> 00:49:33,620
A chum of mine was sledging down claxby hill.

548
00:49:33,800 --> 00:49:37,420
We had a very long, homemade, norwegian-style sledge...

549
00:49:37,590 --> 00:49:40,050
No, not there. over here.

550
00:49:40,680 --> 00:49:42,220
No, sit beside me.

551
00:49:43,970 --> 00:49:45,250
Okay.

552
00:49:46,730 --> 00:49:48,100
Something to drink?

553
00:49:48,270 --> 00:49:50,810
Three butterbeers, and some ginger in mine, please.

554
00:50:02,580 --> 00:50:04,530
Oh, bloody hell.

555
00:50:07,500 --> 00:50:09,320
Slick git.

556
00:50:09,670 --> 00:50:12,340
Honestly, Ronald, they're only holding hands.

557
00:50:15,170 --> 00:50:16,420
And snogging.

558
00:50:17,090 --> 00:50:20,040
- I'd like to leave. - What?

559
00:50:20,220 --> 00:50:21,800
You can't be serious.

560
00:50:21,970 --> 00:50:24,340
- That happens to be my sister. - So?

561
00:50:24,520 --> 00:50:27,120
What if she looked over here and saw you snogging me?

562
00:50:27,120 --> 00:50:28,430
You expect her to leave?

563
00:50:29,730 --> 00:50:32,180
- Hey, my boy! - Hello, sir. Wonderful to see you.

564
00:50:32,360 --> 00:50:34,350
And you, and you.

565
00:50:34,530 --> 00:50:36,320
So, what brings you here?

566
00:50:36,490 --> 00:50:38,000
The three broomsticks and I go way back,

567
00:50:38,000 --> 00:50:41,190
further than I care to admit.

568
00:50:41,370 --> 00:50:44,820
I can remember when it was one broomstick.

569
00:50:44,990 --> 00:50:48,330
All hands on deck, Granger. Listen, my boy, in the old days...

570
00:50:48,500 --> 00:50:51,910
...I used to throw together the occasional supper party...

571
00:50:52,080 --> 00:50:54,290
...for the select student or two.

572
00:50:54,460 --> 00:50:58,330
- Would you be game? - I'd consider it an honor, sir.

573
00:50:59,760 --> 00:51:01,960
You would be welcome too, Granger.

574
00:51:02,760 --> 00:51:07,510
- I'd be delighted, sir. - Splendid. Look for my owl.

575
00:51:08,390 --> 00:51:10,350
Good to see you, Wallenby.

576
00:51:15,270 --> 00:51:16,980
What are you playing at?

577
00:51:18,780 --> 00:51:21,100
Dumbledore's asked me to get to know him.

578
00:51:21,280 --> 00:51:23,240
- Get to know him? - I don't know.

579
00:51:23,410 --> 00:51:24,770
It must be important.

580
00:51:24,770 --> 00:51:27,160
If it wasn't, Dumbledore wouldn't ask.

581
00:51:32,750 --> 00:51:34,870
Got a little bit...

582
00:51:45,760 --> 00:51:47,640
Katie, you don't know what it could be.

583
00:51:47,810 --> 00:51:49,270
- Harry. - what?

584
00:51:49,430 --> 00:51:51,180
Did you hear what she said back at the pub

585
00:51:51,180 --> 00:51:52,930
About me and her snogging?

586
00:51:53,730 --> 00:51:55,470
As if.

587
00:52:01,900 --> 00:52:05,240
I warned her. I warned her not to touch it.

588
00:52:26,720 --> 00:52:29,470
Don't get any closer. Get back, all of you.

589
00:52:41,990 --> 00:52:46,810
Do not touch that, except by the wrappings. do you understand?

590
00:53:00,300 --> 00:53:02,870
You're sure Katie did not have this in her possession...

591
00:53:03,050 --> 00:53:05,540
...when she entered the three broomsticks?

592
00:53:06,180 --> 00:53:07,720
It's like I said.

593
00:53:07,930 --> 00:53:12,840
She left to go to the loo, and when she came back she had the package.

594
00:53:14,100 --> 00:53:16,810
She said it was important that she deliver it.

595
00:53:17,650 --> 00:53:21,150
- Did she say to whom? - To professor Dumbledore.

596
00:53:21,480 --> 00:53:24,150
Very well. Thank you, Leanne. you may go.

597
00:53:28,870 --> 00:53:34,370
Why is it when something happens it is always you three?

598
00:53:35,460 --> 00:53:36,630
Believe me, professor,

599
00:53:36,630 --> 00:53:39,870
I've been asking myself the same question for six years.

600
00:53:40,420 --> 00:53:42,000
Oh, Severus.

601
00:53:47,720 --> 00:53:49,590
What do you think?

602
00:53:51,510 --> 00:53:56,310
I think Miss Bell is lucky to be alive.

603
00:53:56,480 --> 00:53:58,720
She was cursed, wasn't she?

604
00:53:58,900 --> 00:53:59,670
I know Katie.

605
00:53:59,670 --> 00:54:01,570
Off the pitch, she wouldn't hurt a fly.

606
00:54:02,070 --> 00:54:04,620
If she was delivering that to Dumbledore,

607
00:54:04,630 --> 00:54:05,650
She wasn't doing it knowingly.

608
00:54:05,820 --> 00:54:07,730
Yes, she was cursed.

609
00:54:08,530 --> 00:54:10,190
It was Malfoy.

610
00:54:12,120 --> 00:54:15,900
That is a very serious accusation, Potter.

611
00:54:16,080 --> 00:54:17,570
Indeed.

612
00:54:18,420 --> 00:54:21,830
- Your evidence? - I just know.

613
00:54:22,590 --> 00:54:24,580
You just...

614
00:54:25,800 --> 00:54:27,210
...know.

615
00:54:30,260 --> 00:54:32,170
You astonish with your gifts, Potter.

616
00:54:32,350 --> 00:54:36,300
Gifts mere mortals can only dream of possessing.

617
00:54:36,480 --> 00:54:42,600
How grand it must be to be the chosen one.

618
00:54:47,280 --> 00:54:50,780
I suggest you go back to your dormitories. all of you.

619
00:55:01,290 --> 00:55:04,210
What do you suppose Dean sees in her? Ginny?

620
00:55:05,920 --> 00:55:07,910
Well, what does she see in him?

621
00:55:08,090 --> 00:55:10,300
Dean? he's brilliant.

622
00:55:10,470 --> 00:55:13,300
You called him a slick git not five hours ago.

623
00:55:13,470 --> 00:55:17,250
Yeah, well, he was running his hands all over my sister, wasn't he?

624
00:55:17,430 --> 00:55:20,120
Something snaps, and you've gotta hate him, you know?

625
00:55:20,130 --> 00:55:21,980
On principle.

626
00:55:22,650 --> 00:55:24,140
I suppose.

627
00:55:25,400 --> 00:55:28,570
- So, what is it he sees in her? - I don't know.

628
00:55:29,320 --> 00:55:31,730
She's smart, funny.

629
00:55:32,490 --> 00:55:34,780
- Attractive. - Attractive?

630
00:55:36,330 --> 00:55:39,830
- You know, she's got nice skin. - Skin?

631
00:55:40,660 --> 00:55:42,490
Dean dates my sister because of her skin?

632
00:55:42,670 --> 00:55:47,160
Well, no, I mean, I'm just saying it could be a contributing factor.

633
00:55:50,550 --> 00:55:52,290
Hermione's got nice skin.

634
00:55:53,010 --> 00:55:55,760
Wouldn't you say? As skin goes, I mean.

635
00:55:56,720 --> 00:55:58,800
I've never really thought about it.

636
00:56:00,350 --> 00:56:02,060
But, I suppose, yeah.

637
00:56:02,810 --> 00:56:04,270
Very nice.

638
00:56:08,690 --> 00:56:12,060
- I think I'll be going to sleep now. - Right. yeah.

639
00:56:21,910 --> 00:56:23,630
So tell me, Cormac,

640
00:56:23,630 --> 00:56:25,860
Do you see anything of your uncle Tiberius these days?

641
00:56:26,040 --> 00:56:28,530
Yes, sir. In fact, I'm meant to go hunting with him...

642
00:56:28,710 --> 00:56:30,920
...and the minister for magic over the holidays.

643
00:56:31,090 --> 00:56:34,040
Well, be sure to give them both my best.

644
00:56:34,220 --> 00:56:36,210
What about your uncle, Belby?

645
00:56:36,390 --> 00:56:37,970
For those who don't know,

646
00:56:37,970 --> 00:56:39,840
Marcus' uncle invented the wolfsbane potion.

647
00:56:40,020 --> 00:56:42,800
- Is he working on anything new? - Don't know.

648
00:56:42,980 --> 00:56:44,280
Him and dad don't get on.

649
00:56:44,280 --> 00:56:47,060
Probably because me dad says potions are rubbish.

650
00:56:47,230 --> 00:56:48,540
Says the only potion worth having is a stiff

651
00:56:48,550 --> 00:56:50,520
one at the end of the day.

652
00:56:50,690 --> 00:56:52,610
What about you, miss Granger?

653
00:56:52,610 --> 00:56:55,820
What does your family do in the muggle world?

654
00:56:56,570 --> 00:56:58,400
My parents are dentists.

655
00:57:02,960 --> 00:57:04,240
They tend to people's teeth.

656
00:57:04,410 --> 00:57:09,160
Fascinating. and is that considered a dangerous profession?

657
00:57:09,340 --> 00:57:10,620
No.

658
00:57:12,590 --> 00:57:17,090
Although, one boy, Robbie Fenwick, did bite my father once.

659
00:57:17,260 --> 00:57:18,510
He needed 10 stitches.

660
00:57:24,770 --> 00:57:28,390
Ah. miss Weasley. Come in, come in.

661
00:57:31,110 --> 00:57:35,520
Look at her eyes. They've been fighting again, her and dean.

662
00:57:35,700 --> 00:57:38,400
Sorry. I'm not usually late.

663
00:57:42,200 --> 00:57:42,720
No matter.

664
00:57:42,720 --> 00:57:44,390
You're just in time for dessert, that is,

665
00:57:44,390 --> 00:57:46,620
If Belby's left you any.

666
00:57:54,550 --> 00:57:55,630
What?

667
00:57:55,800 --> 00:57:57,420
Nothing.

668
00:58:03,770 --> 00:58:07,380
Goodbye. Bye-bye.

669
00:58:12,270 --> 00:58:14,020
- Potter. - I'm sorry, sir.

670
00:58:14,190 --> 00:58:16,770
I was just admiring your hourglass.

671
00:58:18,160 --> 00:58:19,610
Oh, yes.

672
00:58:20,160 --> 00:58:22,200
A most intriguing object.

673
00:58:22,870 --> 00:58:27,120
The sand runs in accordance with the quality of the conversation.

674
00:58:27,410 --> 00:58:30,660
If it is stimulating, the sand runs slowly.

675
00:58:31,170 --> 00:58:33,080
- If it is not... - I think I'll be going.

676
00:58:33,250 --> 00:58:36,590
Nonsense. You have nothing to fear, dear boy.

677
00:58:36,760 --> 00:58:39,000
As to some of your classmates...

678
00:58:39,180 --> 00:58:42,590
...well, let's just say they're unlikely to make the shelf.

679
00:58:42,760 --> 00:58:44,260
The shelf, sir?

680
00:58:44,850 --> 00:58:48,470
Anyone who aspires to be anyone hopes to end up here.

681
00:58:48,640 --> 00:58:52,510
But then again, you already are someone, aren't you, Harry?

682
00:58:54,070 --> 00:58:56,020
Did Voldemort ever make the shelf, sir?

683
00:58:58,200 --> 00:59:00,990
You knew him, didn't you, sir, Tom Riddle?

684
00:59:00,990 --> 00:59:02,110
You were his teacher.

685
00:59:03,200 --> 00:59:06,700
Mr. Riddle had a number of teachers whilst here at Hogwarts.

686
00:59:06,870 --> 00:59:08,450
What was he like?

687
00:59:12,170 --> 00:59:14,540
I'm sorry, sir. Forgive me.

688
00:59:15,210 --> 00:59:17,040
He killed my parents.

689
00:59:19,800 --> 00:59:21,080
Of course.

690
00:59:21,470 --> 00:59:24,470
It's only natural you should want to know more.

691
00:59:26,560 --> 00:59:29,390
But I'm afraid I must disappoint you, Harry.

692
00:59:30,310 --> 00:59:32,550
When I first met Mr. Riddle, he was a quiet...

693
00:59:32,730 --> 00:59:36,980
...albeit brilliant, boy committed to becoming a first-rate wizard.

694
00:59:37,150 --> 00:59:38,890
Not unlike others I've known.

695
00:59:39,490 --> 00:59:41,560
Not unlike yourself, in fact.

696
00:59:42,910 --> 00:59:44,980
If the monster existed...

697
00:59:45,530 --> 00:59:47,780
...it was buried deep within.

698
01:00:05,100 --> 01:00:06,590
Good luck, eh, Ron.

699
01:00:08,020 --> 01:00:10,470
- Nice hat! - Ron, you're a loser.

700
01:00:10,640 --> 01:00:12,000
I'm counting on you, Ron.

701
01:00:12,000 --> 01:00:13,730
I have two galleons on Gryffindor, yeah?

702
01:00:13,900 --> 01:00:16,220
- Looking good, Ron. - Loser!

703
01:00:18,440 --> 01:00:19,940
What's he wearing?

704
01:00:28,580 --> 01:00:30,400
So how was it, then?

705
01:00:31,620 --> 01:00:33,950
- How was what? - Your dinner party?

706
01:00:34,120 --> 01:00:35,750
Pretty boring, actually.

707
01:00:36,540 --> 01:00:38,870
Though I think Harry enjoyed dessert.

708
01:00:42,300 --> 01:00:45,050
Slughorn's having a christmas do, you know.

709
01:00:45,220 --> 01:00:46,760
And we're meant to bring someone.

710
01:00:46,930 --> 01:00:49,000
I expect you'll be bringing Mclaggen.

711
01:00:49,000 --> 01:00:50,630
He's in the slug club, isn't he?

712
01:00:50,810 --> 01:00:53,640
- Actually, I was going to ask you. - Really?

713
01:00:56,480 --> 01:00:58,470
Good luck today, Ron.

714
01:00:59,320 --> 01:01:01,640
I know you'll be brilliant.

715
01:01:04,700 --> 01:01:08,450
I'm resigning. After today's match, Mclaggen can have my spot.

716
01:01:08,620 --> 01:01:10,110
Have it your way.

717
01:01:10,290 --> 01:01:12,780
- Juice? - Sure.

718
01:01:12,960 --> 01:01:14,660
Hello, everyone.

719
01:01:15,920 --> 01:01:17,990
You look dreadful, Ron.

720
01:01:18,170 --> 01:01:20,540
Is that why you put something in his cup?

721
01:01:22,760 --> 01:01:24,380
Is it a tonic?

722
01:01:27,850 --> 01:01:29,470
Liquid luck.

723
01:01:30,850 --> 01:01:32,510
Don't drink it, Ron.

724
01:01:40,110 --> 01:01:41,550
You could be expelled for that.

725
01:01:41,550 --> 01:01:43,480
I don't know what you're talking about.

726
01:01:45,700 --> 01:01:48,320
Come on, Harry. We've got a game to win.

727
01:02:12,140 --> 01:02:14,050
Yes!

728
01:02:14,470 --> 01:02:17,310
Go on, Ron! Do it!

729
01:02:51,260 --> 01:02:53,550
Weasley! weasley! weasley!

730
01:02:54,010 --> 01:02:55,390
Yes!

731
01:02:55,560 --> 01:02:59,010
Weasley! weasley! weasley!

732
01:03:04,570 --> 01:03:07,770
Yes. whoo!

733
01:03:09,320 --> 01:03:14,360
Weasley! weasley! weasley!

734
01:03:18,620 --> 01:03:20,330
You really shouldn't have done it.

735
01:03:20,500 --> 01:03:25,490
I know. I suppose I could've just used a confundus charm.

736
01:03:26,510 --> 01:03:31,130
That was different. That was tryouts. This was an actual game.

737
01:03:33,930 --> 01:03:35,640
You didn't put it in.

738
01:03:37,350 --> 01:03:39,180
Ron only thought you did.

739
01:04:26,980 --> 01:04:30,270
Charms spell. I'm just practicing.

740
01:04:34,200 --> 01:04:36,020
Well, they're really good.

741
01:04:41,540 --> 01:04:43,530
How does it feel, Harry?

742
01:04:46,380 --> 01:04:49,580
When you see Dean with Ginny?

743
01:04:54,680 --> 01:04:56,140
I know.

744
01:04:57,220 --> 01:04:59,380
I see the way you look at her.

745
01:05:00,100 --> 01:05:01,720
You're my best friend.

746
01:05:14,070 --> 01:05:16,310
I think this room's taken.

747
01:05:18,080 --> 01:05:19,490
What's with the birds?

748
01:05:22,870 --> 01:05:24,580
Oppugno.

749
01:05:52,610 --> 01:05:54,320
It feels like this.

750
01:06:34,030 --> 01:06:37,060
Look, I can't help it if she's got her knickers in a twist.

751
01:06:37,240 --> 01:06:42,310
What Lav and I have, well, let's just say, there's no stopping it.

752
01:06:42,490 --> 01:06:43,900
It's chemical.

753
01:06:44,080 --> 01:06:46,850
Will it last? who knows?

754
01:06:46,850 --> 01:06:48,410
Point is, I'm a free agent.

755
01:06:48,580 --> 01:06:51,420
He's at perfect liberty to kiss whoever he likes.

756
01:06:51,590 --> 01:06:53,990
I really couldn't care less.

757
01:06:54,170 --> 01:06:55,810
Was I under the impression he and I

758
01:06:55,810 --> 01:06:58,000
Would be attending slughorn's christmas party?

759
01:06:58,180 --> 01:06:59,670
Yes.

760
01:06:59,840 --> 01:07:04,260
Now, given the circumstances, I've had to make other arrangements.

761
01:07:04,430 --> 01:07:05,630
Have you?

762
01:07:05,810 --> 01:07:07,800
Yes. why?

763
01:07:07,980 --> 01:07:08,630
I just thought,

764
01:07:08,630 --> 01:07:11,600
Seeing as neither of us can go with who we'd really like to...

765
01:07:11,770 --> 01:07:14,010
...we should go together, as friends.

766
01:07:14,190 --> 01:07:15,820
Why didn't I think of that?

767
01:07:15,980 --> 01:07:17,530
Who are you going with?

768
01:07:17,690 --> 01:07:19,490
Um, it's a surprise.

769
01:07:19,660 --> 01:07:23,870
Anyway, it's you we've got to worry about. you can't just take anyone.

770
01:07:24,490 --> 01:07:26,370
See that girl over there?

771
01:07:28,000 --> 01:07:30,040
That's Romilda Vane.

772
01:07:30,040 --> 01:07:32,710
Apparently she's trying to smuggle you a love potion.

773
01:07:32,880 --> 01:07:34,370
Really?

774
01:07:35,340 --> 01:07:35,480
Hey!

775
01:07:35,480 --> 01:07:36,630
She's only interested in you

776
01:07:36,640 --> 01:07:38,790
Because she thinks you're the chosen one.

777
01:07:38,970 --> 01:07:40,670
But I am the chosen one.

778
01:07:40,840 --> 01:07:43,710
Okay, sorry. um, kidding.

779
01:07:45,720 --> 01:07:47,180
I'll ask someone I like.

780
01:07:47,980 --> 01:07:49,520
Someone cool.

781
01:07:59,280 --> 01:08:02,310
I've never been to this part of the castle.

782
01:08:02,490 --> 01:08:05,740
At least not while awake. I sleepwalk, you see.

783
01:08:05,910 --> 01:08:08,400
That's why I wear shoes to bed.

784
01:08:39,610 --> 01:08:42,610
Harmonia nectere passus.

785
01:08:55,130 --> 01:08:57,880
Harmonia nectere passus.

786
01:08:59,420 --> 01:09:02,090
Harmonia nectere passus.

787
01:09:16,730 --> 01:09:18,140
Drink?

788
01:09:19,070 --> 01:09:20,390
Neville.

789
01:09:20,570 --> 01:09:22,030
I didn't get into the slug club.

790
01:09:22,190 --> 01:09:25,310
It's okay, though. he's got Belby handing out towels in the loo.

791
01:09:25,490 --> 01:09:28,280
- Oh, well, I'm fine, mate. thanks. - Okay.

792
01:09:38,710 --> 01:09:41,660
Hermione. what are you doing? and what happened to you?

793
01:09:41,840 --> 01:09:43,410
I've just escaped.

794
01:09:43,410 --> 01:09:47,130
I mean, left Cormac under the mistletoe.

795
01:09:47,300 --> 01:09:50,340
Cormac? That's who you invited?

796
01:09:50,510 --> 01:09:53,010
I thought it would annoy Ron the most.

797
01:09:53,850 --> 01:09:55,840
Thank you. I'll catch up with you later.

798
01:09:56,020 --> 01:09:59,020
He's got more tentacles than a snarfalump plant.

799
01:09:59,190 --> 01:10:01,350
- Dragon tartare? - No, I'm fine. thank you.

800
01:10:01,530 --> 01:10:04,190
Just as well. they give one horribly bad breath.

801
01:10:04,360 --> 01:10:06,190
On second thoughts...

802
01:10:06,360 --> 01:10:08,360
Might keep Cormac at bay.

803
01:10:08,700 --> 01:10:11,620
Oh, god, here he comes.

804
01:10:14,160 --> 01:10:17,030
I think she just went to powder her nose.

805
01:10:17,210 --> 01:10:19,280
Slippery little minx, your friend.

806
01:10:19,460 --> 01:10:22,160
Likes to work her mouth too, doesn't she?

807
01:10:25,220 --> 01:10:27,210
What is this I'm eating, by the way?

808
01:10:28,390 --> 01:10:30,010
Dragon balls.

809
01:10:41,230 --> 01:10:44,350
You've just bought yourself a month's detention, Mclaggen.

810
01:10:44,530 --> 01:10:48,390
Not so quick, Potter.

811
01:10:49,950 --> 01:10:53,070
Sir, I really think I should rejoin the party. my date...

812
01:10:53,240 --> 01:10:57,160
Can surely survive your absence for another minute or two.

813
01:10:57,330 --> 01:10:59,570
Besides, I only wish to convey a message.

814
01:11:00,210 --> 01:11:02,450
- A message? - From professor dumbledore.

815
01:11:02,630 --> 01:11:06,290
He asked me to give you his best, and he hopes you enjoy your holiday.

816
01:11:06,470 --> 01:11:08,010
You see...

817
01:11:08,180 --> 01:11:13,720
...he's traveling, and he won't return until term resumes.

818
01:11:13,890 --> 01:11:15,430
Traveling where?

819
01:11:23,570 --> 01:11:25,440
Take your hands off me, you filthy squib!

820
01:11:26,570 --> 01:11:28,280
Professor Slughorn, sir.

821
01:11:28,450 --> 01:11:32,770
I just discovered this boy lurking in an upstairs corridor.

822
01:11:32,950 --> 01:11:34,990
He claims to have been invited to your party.

823
01:11:35,160 --> 01:11:38,450
Okay, okay. I was gatecrashing. happy?

824
01:11:38,650 --> 01:11:42,480
I'll escort him out.

825
01:11:45,280 --> 01:11:48,940
Certainly, professor.

826
01:11:52,580 --> 01:11:55,830
All right, everyone, carry on, carry on.

827
01:11:57,920 --> 01:12:02,830
Maybe I did hex that bell girl. maybe I didn't. what's it to you?

828
01:12:03,000 --> 01:12:05,080
I swore to protect you.

829
01:12:05,260 --> 01:12:08,590
I made the unbreakable vow.

830
01:12:08,760 --> 01:12:10,920
I don't need protection.

831
01:12:11,100 --> 01:12:15,260
I was chosen for this. out of all others. me.

832
01:12:16,180 --> 01:12:19,720
- and I won't fail him. - you're afraid, draco.

833
01:12:20,310 --> 01:12:24,230
You attempt to conceal it, but it's obvious. let me assist you.

834
01:12:24,400 --> 01:12:25,860
No!

835
01:12:26,190 --> 01:12:29,610
I was chosen. this is my moment.

836
01:12:42,040 --> 01:12:43,620
"unbreakable vow."

837
01:12:43,790 --> 01:12:45,420
You're sure that's what snape said?

838
01:12:45,590 --> 01:12:47,880
Positive. why?

839
01:12:48,050 --> 01:12:51,550
Well, it's just you can't break an unbreakable vow.

840
01:12:51,720 --> 01:12:55,050
I'd worked that much out for myself, funnily enough.

841
01:12:55,560 --> 01:12:57,300
You don't understand.

842
01:12:57,930 --> 01:12:58,970
Oh, bloody hell.

843
01:13:26,800 --> 01:13:28,750
I miss you.

844
01:13:30,470 --> 01:13:32,010
Lovely.

845
01:13:32,180 --> 01:13:35,460
All she wants to do is snog me. my lips are getting chapped. look.

846
01:13:35,640 --> 01:13:37,840
I'll take your word for it.

847
01:13:47,940 --> 01:13:52,900
So, what happens to you? what happens if you break an unbreakable vow?

848
01:13:53,450 --> 01:13:55,160
You die.

849
01:13:59,750 --> 01:14:01,620
Wait, the pudding's still here.

850
01:14:02,870 --> 01:14:06,210
Voldemort has chosen Draco Malfoy for a mission?

851
01:14:06,380 --> 01:14:07,460
I know it sounds mad.

852
01:14:07,630 --> 01:14:11,130
Has it occurred to you snape was simply pretending to offer draco help...

853
01:14:11,300 --> 01:14:13,790
...so he could find out what he was up to?

854
01:14:13,970 --> 01:14:16,970
- that's not what it sounded like. - perhaps harry's right.

855
01:14:17,510 --> 01:14:19,140
To make an unbreakable vow, it's...

856
01:14:19,310 --> 01:14:22,810
It comes down to whether or not you trust dumbledore's judgment.

857
01:14:22,980 --> 01:14:27,060
- Dumbledore trusts snape, therefore I do. - Dumbledore can make mistakes.

858
01:14:27,230 --> 01:14:28,390
You're blinded by hatred.

859
01:14:28,570 --> 01:14:30,610
- I'm not. - yes, you are.

860
01:14:32,360 --> 01:14:35,360
People are disappearing, harry, daily.

861
01:14:35,530 --> 01:14:37,490
We place our trust in a handful of people.

862
01:14:37,660 --> 01:14:40,610
If we start fighting amongst ourselves, we're doomed.

863
01:15:05,100 --> 01:15:06,650
Open up, you.

864
01:15:08,310 --> 01:15:09,940
Don't you trust me?

865
01:15:16,200 --> 01:15:17,280
It's good.

866
01:15:18,200 --> 01:15:21,030
Yeah, I'll just... get... yeah.

867
01:15:27,790 --> 01:15:30,580
- pie? - not for me, no.

868
01:15:42,520 --> 01:15:44,060
You'll have to forgive remus.

869
01:15:44,310 --> 01:15:47,140
It takes its toll, his condition.

870
01:15:48,060 --> 01:15:50,100
Are you all right, mr. weasley?

871
01:15:50,270 --> 01:15:52,810
We're being followed, all of us.

872
01:15:52,980 --> 01:15:55,480
Most days, Molly doesn't leave the house.

873
01:15:56,320 --> 01:15:58,400
It's not been easy.

874
01:16:00,410 --> 01:16:01,820
Did you get my owl?

875
01:16:01,990 --> 01:16:04,070
Yes, I did.

876
01:16:05,580 --> 01:16:08,620
If dumbledore's traveling, then that's news to the ministry...

877
01:16:08,790 --> 01:16:11,250
...but perhaps that's the way dumbledore wants it.

878
01:16:11,960 --> 01:16:14,450
As for draco malfoy...

879
01:16:15,090 --> 01:16:16,250
...i know a bit more.

880
01:16:16,880 --> 01:16:19,920
- go on. - I sent an agent to Borgin and Burkes.

881
01:16:20,090 --> 01:16:22,420
I think, from what you described...

882
01:16:22,600 --> 01:16:24,260
...what you and Ron saw in summer...

883
01:16:24,430 --> 01:16:27,930
...the object that Draco is so interested in...

884
01:16:28,100 --> 01:16:29,600
...is a vanishing cabinet.

885
01:16:30,480 --> 01:16:31,760
A vanishing cabinet?

886
01:16:31,940 --> 01:16:35,940
They were all the rage when Voldemort first rose to power.

887
01:16:36,110 --> 01:16:39,060
You can see the appeal. should death eaters come knocking...

888
01:16:39,240 --> 01:16:43,980
...one simply had to slip inside and disappear for an hour or two.

889
01:16:44,620 --> 01:16:46,360
They can transport you anywhere.

890
01:16:46,540 --> 01:16:49,910
Tricky contraptions though, very temperamental.

891
01:16:50,080 --> 01:16:53,000
What happened to it? the one at borgin and burkes?

892
01:16:53,170 --> 01:16:54,280
Nothing.

893
01:16:55,130 --> 01:16:56,840
It's still there.

894
01:17:07,930 --> 01:17:09,640
It was delicious, Molly, really.

895
01:17:09,810 --> 01:17:11,140
Are you sure you won't stay?

896
01:17:11,310 --> 01:17:15,690
No, we should go. the first night of the cycle's always the worst.

897
01:17:15,860 --> 01:17:16,890
Remus?

898
01:17:25,830 --> 01:17:27,370
Sweetheart.

899
01:17:35,670 --> 01:17:37,410
Has Ron gone to bed?

900
01:17:37,590 --> 01:17:40,420
Um... not yet. no.

901
01:17:42,220 --> 01:17:43,550
Shoelace.

902
01:17:56,150 --> 01:17:58,020
Merry christmas, Harry.

903
01:17:59,440 --> 01:18:00,990
Merry christmas.

904
01:18:18,250 --> 01:18:20,540
- Harry, no! - Remus!

905
01:18:30,390 --> 01:18:31,800
Ginny!

906
01:18:34,980 --> 01:18:39,640
I killed Sirius Black! I killed sirius black!

907
01:18:39,820 --> 01:18:42,060
You coming to get me?

908
01:18:43,150 --> 01:18:46,490
Harry, can you get me? you coming to get me?

909
01:19:16,230 --> 01:19:17,600
Harry?

910
01:19:35,120 --> 01:19:36,780
Stupefy!

911
01:19:59,650 --> 01:20:01,390
Harry!

912
01:20:14,910 --> 01:20:16,110
Ginny!

913
01:20:45,690 --> 01:20:47,190
Molly.

914
01:21:10,180 --> 01:21:11,880
It's easy for them to get to you.

915
01:21:12,050 --> 01:21:14,040
You're bloody lucky you weren't killed.

916
01:21:14,040 --> 01:21:16,180
You have to realize who you are, Harry.

917
01:21:16,350 --> 01:21:18,890
I know who I am, Hermione, all right?

918
01:21:19,850 --> 01:21:21,050
Sorry.

919
01:21:22,730 --> 01:21:26,060
Lav, come on. of course I'll wear it.

920
01:21:26,230 --> 01:21:28,390
That's my won-won.

921
01:21:30,400 --> 01:21:32,810
Excuse me, I have to go and vomit.

922
01:21:50,470 --> 01:21:52,760
I'd like to know where you get your information.

923
01:21:52,930 --> 01:21:55,960
More knowledgeable than half the staff, you are.

924
01:22:01,600 --> 01:22:03,140
Sir...

925
01:22:03,600 --> 01:22:06,440
...is it true that professor Merrythought is retiring?

926
01:22:06,610 --> 01:22:09,390
Now, Tom. I couldn't tell you if I knew, could i?

927
01:22:09,650 --> 01:22:11,710
By the way, thank you for the pineapple.

928
01:22:11,710 --> 01:22:13,820
You're quite right, it is my favorite.

929
01:22:14,410 --> 01:22:16,700
But how did you know?

930
01:22:18,540 --> 01:22:20,110
Intuition.

931
01:22:24,290 --> 01:22:26,000
Gracious. is it that time already?

932
01:22:26,170 --> 01:22:29,830
Off you go, boys, or professor Dippet will have us all in detention.

933
01:22:33,970 --> 01:22:37,800
Look sharp, Tom. don't want to be caught out of bed after hours.

934
01:22:39,720 --> 01:22:41,800
- is something on your mind, tom? - yes, sir.

935
01:22:43,140 --> 01:22:45,980
You see, I couldn't think of anyone else to go to.

936
01:22:46,900 --> 01:22:51,890
The other professors, well, they're not like you.

937
01:22:52,280 --> 01:22:55,310
They might misunderstand.

938
01:22:55,490 --> 01:22:57,070
Go on.

939
01:22:57,870 --> 01:23:00,160
I was in the library the other night...

940
01:23:00,700 --> 01:23:02,910
...in the restricted section...

941
01:23:03,660 --> 01:23:07,200
...and I read something rather odd about a bit of rare magic.

942
01:23:08,130 --> 01:23:11,630
And I thought perhaps you could illuminate me.

943
01:23:11,800 --> 01:23:14,590
It's called, as I understand it...

944
01:23:17,510 --> 01:23:18,670
I beg your pardon?

945
01:23:18,850 --> 01:23:21,380
I don't know anything about such things, and if I did,

946
01:23:21,380 --> 01:23:22,430
I wouldn't tell you!

947
01:23:22,600 --> 01:23:24,240
Now, get out of here at once,

948
01:23:24,240 --> 01:23:27,390
And don't let me ever catch you mentioning it again!

949
01:23:30,360 --> 01:23:31,520
Confused?

950
01:23:32,190 --> 01:23:33,690
I'd be surprised if you weren't.

951
01:23:34,610 --> 01:23:37,360
Well, I don't understand. what happened?

952
01:23:37,530 --> 01:23:41,200
This is perhaps the most important memory I've collected.

953
01:23:41,540 --> 01:23:43,280
It is also a lie.

954
01:23:44,210 --> 01:23:46,000
This memory has been tampered with...

955
01:23:46,280 --> 01:23:50,540
By the same person whose memory it is, our old friend, professor Slughorn.

956
01:23:51,170 --> 01:23:53,160
But why would he tamper with his own memory?

957
01:23:53,340 --> 01:23:56,210
- I suspect he's ashamed of it. - why?

958
01:23:56,380 --> 01:23:57,880
Why, indeed?

959
01:23:58,680 --> 01:24:02,050
I asked you to get to know professor slughorn, and you have done so.

960
01:24:02,220 --> 01:24:05,840
Now I want you to persuade him to divulge his true memory...

961
01:24:06,020 --> 01:24:07,560
...any way you can.

962
01:24:07,730 --> 01:24:09,690
I don't know him that well, sir.

963
01:24:14,150 --> 01:24:17,070
This memory is everything.

964
01:24:17,570 --> 01:24:19,560
Without it, we are blind.

965
01:24:20,070 --> 01:24:23,690
Without it, we leave the fate of our world to chance.

966
01:24:25,750 --> 01:24:27,570
You have no choice.

967
01:24:28,790 --> 01:24:30,780
You must not fail.

968
01:24:38,890 --> 01:24:41,210
So I'd highly recommend you reacquaint yourself...

969
01:24:41,390 --> 01:24:42,850
...with the chapter on antidotes.

970
01:24:43,010 --> 01:24:46,760
I'll tell you more about bezoars in our next class. right, off you go.

971
01:24:46,930 --> 01:24:49,430
Alys, don't forget your rat tail.

972
01:24:54,900 --> 01:24:58,690
Aha. if it isn't the prince of potions himself.

973
01:24:58,860 --> 01:25:00,770
To what do I owe this pleasure?

974
01:25:01,950 --> 01:25:04,030
Sir, I wondered if I might ask you something.

975
01:25:04,200 --> 01:25:06,440
Ask away, dear boy, ask away.

976
01:25:06,620 --> 01:25:09,620
The other day I was in the library, in the restricted section...

977
01:25:09,890 --> 01:25:13,460
And I came across something rather odd about a very rare piece of magic.

978
01:25:14,800 --> 01:25:17,470
Yes. and what was this rare piece of magic?

979
01:25:17,630 --> 01:25:20,970
Well, I don't know. I can't remember the name exactly.

980
01:25:21,140 --> 01:25:22,140
It got me wondering,

981
01:25:22,140 --> 01:25:25,460
Are there some kinds of magic you're not allowed to teach us?

982
01:25:27,480 --> 01:25:28,800
I'm potions master, Harry.

983
01:25:28,980 --> 01:25:31,810
I think your question'd better be posed to professor Snape.

984
01:25:31,980 --> 01:25:33,890
Yes. um...

985
01:25:34,070 --> 01:25:36,560
He and I don't exactly see eye to eye, sir.

986
01:25:36,730 --> 01:25:38,530
What I mean to say is...

987
01:25:39,360 --> 01:25:41,150
...well, he's not like you.

988
01:25:41,820 --> 01:25:43,650
He might misunderstand.

989
01:25:44,950 --> 01:25:48,780
Yes. there can be no light without the dark.

990
01:25:48,960 --> 01:25:53,000
And so it is with magic. myself, I always strive to live within the light.

991
01:25:53,630 --> 01:25:55,290
I suggest you do the same.

992
01:25:55,670 --> 01:25:58,670
Is that what you told Tom Riddle, when he came asking questions?

993
01:26:05,640 --> 01:26:08,670
Dumbledore put you up to this, didn't he?

994
01:26:10,690 --> 01:26:12,310
Didn't he?

995
01:26:19,690 --> 01:26:20,970
Yes?

996
01:26:21,360 --> 01:26:23,490
Oh, it's you, Potter.

997
01:26:23,660 --> 01:26:26,030
I'm sorry, I'm busy at the moment.

998
01:26:38,840 --> 01:26:42,620
It's beautiful, isn't it? the moon.

999
01:26:43,630 --> 01:26:45,050
Divine.

1000
01:26:45,720 --> 01:26:48,010
Had ourselves a little late-night snack, did we?

1001
01:26:49,140 --> 01:26:52,720
It was on your bed, the box. I just thought I'd try one.

1002
01:26:52,890 --> 01:26:56,390
- or 20. - I can't stop thinking about her, harry.

1003
01:26:56,560 --> 01:26:58,560
Honestly, I reckoned she was annoying you.

1004
01:26:58,730 --> 01:27:01,060
She could never annoy me.

1005
01:27:02,860 --> 01:27:04,400
I think I love her.

1006
01:27:07,990 --> 01:27:10,280
Well, brilliant.

1007
01:27:14,120 --> 01:27:15,750
Do you think she knows I exist?

1008
01:27:15,920 --> 01:27:18,410
I hope so. she's been snogging you for three months.

1009
01:27:18,590 --> 01:27:21,540
Snogging? who are you talking about?

1010
01:27:22,470 --> 01:27:23,710
Who are you talking about?

1011
01:27:24,470 --> 01:27:28,090
Romilda, of course. Romilda Vane.

1012
01:27:28,260 --> 01:27:29,760
Okay, very funny.

1013
01:27:32,890 --> 01:27:36,560
- what was that for? - it's no joke! I'm in love with her!

1014
01:27:36,730 --> 01:27:39,600
Fine, you're in love with her. have you ever actually met her?

1015
01:27:40,570 --> 01:27:43,520
No. can you introduce me?

1016
01:28:05,220 --> 01:28:09,960
Come on, ron. I'm gonna introduce you to Romilda Vanee.

1017
01:28:20,730 --> 01:28:24,430
I'm sorry, sir. I wouldn't bother you if it weren't absolutely essential.

1018
01:28:25,280 --> 01:28:26,690
Where's Romilda?

1019
01:28:26,860 --> 01:28:28,820
What's the matter with wenby?

1020
01:28:29,320 --> 01:28:31,150
Very powerful love potion.

1021
01:28:31,330 --> 01:28:33,700
Very well. better bring him in.

1022
01:28:33,870 --> 01:28:37,160
I'd have thought you could whip up a remedy for this in no time, Harry.

1023
01:28:37,330 --> 01:28:40,250
Well, I thought this called for a more practiced hand, sir.

1024
01:28:40,420 --> 01:28:43,500
Hello, darling. fancy a drink?

1025
01:28:43,670 --> 01:28:45,330
Perhaps you're right.

1026
01:28:49,840 --> 01:28:53,630
I'm sorry, by the way, professor, about earlier today,

1027
01:28:53,630 --> 01:28:55,270
Our misunderstanding.

1028
01:28:55,430 --> 01:28:59,810
Oh, not at all. all water under the bridge, you know? correct?

1029
01:28:59,980 --> 01:29:02,900
I expect you're tired of it after all these years.

1030
01:29:03,070 --> 01:29:05,640
All the questions about voldemort.

1031
01:29:05,820 --> 01:29:07,650
Don't use that name.

1032
01:29:15,370 --> 01:29:17,450
There you are, old boy. bottoms up.

1033
01:29:17,620 --> 01:29:20,740
- what's this? - tonic for the nerves.

1034
01:29:35,260 --> 01:29:37,550
- what happened to me? - love potion.

1035
01:29:37,730 --> 01:29:39,850
A bloody strong one at that.

1036
01:29:40,440 --> 01:29:44,050
- I feel really bad. - you need a pick-me-up.

1037
01:29:44,230 --> 01:29:47,900
Got butterbeer, wine, dazzling oak-matured mead.

1038
01:29:48,070 --> 01:29:52,400
I had other intentions for this, but I think, given the circumstances...

1039
01:29:54,700 --> 01:29:56,410
Here we are, potter.

1040
01:29:56,580 --> 01:29:58,070
To life!

1041
01:30:02,880 --> 01:30:03,910
Ron.

1042
01:30:06,380 --> 01:30:09,830
Ron. professor, do something.

1043
01:30:10,930 --> 01:30:12,550
I don't understand.

1044
01:30:28,940 --> 01:30:30,730
Come on, ron, breathe.

1045
01:30:52,970 --> 01:30:55,800
These girls, they're gonna kill me.

1046
01:31:06,810 --> 01:31:10,180
Quick thinking on your part, harry, using a bezoar.

1047
01:31:10,360 --> 01:31:12,730
You must be very proud of your student, Horace.

1048
01:31:12,900 --> 01:31:16,320
Hm? oh, yes, very proud.

1049
01:31:16,490 --> 01:31:19,240
I think we agree, potter's actions were heroic.

1050
01:31:19,410 --> 01:31:23,410
The question is, why were they necessary?

1051
01:31:23,580 --> 01:31:25,320
Why, indeed?

1052
01:31:25,500 --> 01:31:27,490
This appears to be a gift, Horace.

1053
01:31:27,840 --> 01:31:30,670
You don't remember who gave you this bottle?

1054
01:31:30,840 --> 01:31:31,700
Which, by the way,

1055
01:31:31,700 --> 01:31:34,790
Possesses remarkably subtle hints of licorice and cherry...

1056
01:31:34,970 --> 01:31:37,420
...when not polluted with poison.

1057
01:31:37,600 --> 01:31:40,720
Actually I had intended to give it as a gift myself.

1058
01:31:40,890 --> 01:31:42,270
To whom, I might ask?

1059
01:31:44,100 --> 01:31:46,260
To you, headmaster.

1060
01:31:48,610 --> 01:31:49,690
Where is he?

1061
01:31:49,860 --> 01:31:53,990
Where's my won-won? has he been asking for me?

1062
01:31:57,030 --> 01:31:58,690
What's she doing here?

1063
01:31:58,870 --> 01:32:01,110
I might ask you the same question.

1064
01:32:01,290 --> 01:32:03,530
I happen to be his girlfriend.

1065
01:32:03,700 --> 01:32:06,460
I happen to be his...friend.

1066
01:32:06,620 --> 01:32:10,840
Don't make me laugh. You haven't spoken in weeks.

1067
01:32:11,630 --> 01:32:14,500
I suppose you want to make up now that he's all interesting.

1068
01:32:14,670 --> 01:32:18,370
He's been poisoned, you daft dimbo!

1069
01:32:18,550 --> 01:32:21,390
And for the record, I've always found him interesting.

1070
01:32:23,060 --> 01:32:28,100
Ah. see? He senses my presence.

1071
01:32:28,270 --> 01:32:31,560
Don't worry, won-won. I'm here.

1072
01:32:32,230 --> 01:32:34,060
I'm here.

1073
01:32:39,910 --> 01:32:43,110
Uh... Hermione...

1074
01:32:47,170 --> 01:32:49,160
Hermione.

1075
01:32:49,920 --> 01:32:52,160
Hermione.

1076
01:32:59,760 --> 01:33:03,680
Oh, to be young, and to feel love's keen sting.

1077
01:33:04,020 --> 01:33:06,340
Well, come away, everybody.

1078
01:33:06,520 --> 01:33:09,140
Mr. weasley is well tended.

1079
01:33:13,400 --> 01:33:15,940
About time, don't you think?

1080
01:33:18,610 --> 01:33:20,190
Thank you.

1081
01:33:23,120 --> 01:33:24,940
Oh, shut up.

1082
01:35:37,250 --> 01:35:41,040
Stop it, Ron. You're making it snow.

1083
01:35:45,510 --> 01:35:48,180
Tell me how I broke up with Lavender again.

1084
01:35:52,020 --> 01:35:55,020
...she came to visit you in the hospital.

1085
01:35:55,900 --> 01:35:58,300
And you talked.

1086
01:35:59,900 --> 01:36:03,980
I don't believe it was a particularly long conversation.

1087
01:36:04,150 --> 01:36:07,440
Don't get me wrong, I'm bloody thrilled to be shot of her.

1088
01:36:07,620 --> 01:36:09,940
It's just she seems a bit put out.

1089
01:36:16,460 --> 01:36:19,960
Yes, she does, doesn't she?

1090
01:36:21,590 --> 01:36:26,630
You say you don't remember anything from that night?

1091
01:36:26,800 --> 01:36:29,800
Anything at all?

1092
01:36:29,970 --> 01:36:31,800
There is something.

1093
01:36:35,310 --> 01:36:39,770
But it can't be. I was completely boggled, wasn't i?

1094
01:36:41,270 --> 01:36:44,480
Right. boggled.

1095
01:36:51,740 --> 01:36:52,990
Harry.

1096
01:36:54,450 --> 01:36:55,620
That's Katie.

1097
01:36:57,580 --> 01:36:59,210
Katie Bell.

1098
01:37:06,880 --> 01:37:09,260
Katie. How are you?

1099
01:37:09,930 --> 01:37:14,420
I know you're going to ask, Harry, but I don't know who cursed me.

1100
01:37:16,060 --> 01:37:19,590
I've been trying to remember, honestly.

1101
01:37:20,020 --> 01:37:23,440
But I just can't.

1102
01:37:36,700 --> 01:37:38,030
Katie?

1103
01:38:20,500 --> 01:38:24,580
I know what you did, malfoy. You hexed her, didn't you?

1104
01:38:54,950 --> 01:38:56,940
Sectumsempra!

1105
01:39:43,920 --> 01:39:46,830
Vulnera sanentur.

1106
01:39:48,500 --> 01:39:51,340
Vulnera sanentur.

1107
01:39:53,630 --> 01:39:56,500
Vulnera sanentur.

1108
01:40:17,620 --> 01:40:21,150
You have to get rid of it. today.

1109
01:40:26,040 --> 01:40:27,670
Take my hand.

1110
01:40:43,640 --> 01:40:45,550
The room of requirement.

1111
01:40:52,020 --> 01:40:54,650
We need to hide the half-blood prince's book...

1112
01:40:54,820 --> 01:40:58,520
...Where no one will ever find it, including you.

1113
01:41:06,870 --> 01:41:08,330
- What was that? - what was that?

1114
01:41:34,440 --> 01:41:35,770
See?

1115
01:41:36,320 --> 01:41:38,360
You never know what you'll find up here.

1116
01:41:57,510 --> 01:42:01,420
All right, close your eyes. that way you can't be tempted.

1117
01:42:05,260 --> 01:42:06,970
Close your eyes.

1118
01:42:33,670 --> 01:42:36,540
That can stay hidden up here too, if you like.

1119
01:42:51,190 --> 01:42:53,560
So did you and Ginny do it, then?

1120
01:42:53,730 --> 01:42:54,890
What?

1121
01:42:55,060 --> 01:42:57,140
You know, hide the book?

1122
01:42:57,320 --> 01:42:59,190
Oh, yeah.

1123
01:43:02,110 --> 01:43:04,690
Ah. dear, yes.

1124
01:43:04,870 --> 01:43:07,650
Still no luck with Slughorn, then, I take it?

1125
01:43:09,700 --> 01:43:11,030
Luck.

1126
01:43:12,080 --> 01:43:15,420
That's it. all I need's a bit of luck.

1127
01:43:33,560 --> 01:43:36,760
Well, how do you feel?

1128
01:43:36,940 --> 01:43:38,560
Excellent.

1129
01:43:39,730 --> 01:43:41,730
Really excellent.

1130
01:43:44,490 --> 01:43:46,070
Remember...

1131
01:43:46,410 --> 01:43:48,150
...Sughorn usually eats early...

1132
01:43:48,330 --> 01:43:51,330
...takes a walk, and then returns to his office.

1133
01:43:51,500 --> 01:43:52,990
Right.

1134
01:43:53,410 --> 01:43:55,570
- I'm going down to hagrid's. - What?

1135
01:43:55,750 --> 01:43:58,420
No, Harry, you've got to go and speak to Slughorn.

1136
01:44:00,000 --> 01:44:02,580
- we have a plan. - I know...

1137
01:44:02,760 --> 01:44:04,830
...but I've got a good feeling about Hagrid's.

1138
01:44:05,010 --> 01:44:08,760
I feel it's the place to be tonight. do you know what I mean?

1139
01:44:09,640 --> 01:44:11,880
- No. - Well, trust me, I know what I'm doing.

1140
01:44:12,060 --> 01:44:14,220
Or felix does.

1141
01:44:15,350 --> 01:44:16,850
Hi!

1142
01:44:47,470 --> 01:44:49,180
Merlin's beard, harry!

1143
01:44:49,350 --> 01:44:50,350
Sorry, sir.

1144
01:44:50,350 --> 01:44:53,470
I should've announced myself. cleared my throat, coughed.

1145
01:44:53,640 --> 01:44:55,600
You probably feared I was Professor Sprout.

1146
01:44:55,770 --> 01:44:59,180
Yes, I did, actually. what makes you think that?

1147
01:44:59,360 --> 01:45:01,430
Well, just the general behavior, sir.

1148
01:45:01,610 --> 01:45:04,390
The sneaking around, the jumping when you saw me.

1149
01:45:04,570 --> 01:45:08,150
Are those tentacula leaves, sir? they're very valuable, aren't they?

1150
01:45:08,320 --> 01:45:10,650
Ten galleons a leaf to the right buyer.

1151
01:45:10,830 --> 01:45:13,070
Not that I'm familiar with any such transactions,

1152
01:45:13,070 --> 01:45:14,320
But one does hear rumors.

1153
01:45:14,500 --> 01:45:18,280
My own interests are purely academic, of course.

1154
01:45:18,460 --> 01:45:21,740
Personally, these plants always kind of freaked me out.

1155
01:45:25,010 --> 01:45:27,160
How did you get out of the castle, harry?

1156
01:45:27,340 --> 01:45:28,840
Through the front door, sir.

1157
01:45:29,010 --> 01:45:31,170
I'm off to Hagrid's. he's a very dear friend...

1158
01:45:31,350 --> 01:45:33,050
...and I fancied paying him a visit.

1159
01:45:33,220 --> 01:45:35,510
So if you don't mind, I will be going now.

1160
01:45:36,310 --> 01:45:37,930
Harry!

1161
01:45:38,770 --> 01:45:41,230
- sir? - it's nearly nightfall.

1162
01:45:41,400 --> 01:45:43,050
Surely you realize I can't allow you

1163
01:45:43,050 --> 01:45:44,850
To go roaming the grounds by yourself.

1164
01:45:45,030 --> 01:45:47,600
Well, then, by all means, come along, sir.

1165
01:45:52,950 --> 01:45:56,150
Harry, I must insist you accompany me...

1166
01:45:56,330 --> 01:45:58,070
...Back to the castle immediately!

1167
01:45:58,250 --> 01:46:01,500
That would be counterproductive, sir.

1168
01:46:02,840 --> 01:46:04,960
And what makes you say that?

1169
01:46:06,050 --> 01:46:07,620
No idea.

1170
01:46:14,390 --> 01:46:15,800
Horace.

1171
01:46:16,430 --> 01:46:21,720
Merlin's beard. Is that an actual acromantula?

1172
01:46:22,310 --> 01:46:24,390
A dead one, I think, sir.

1173
01:46:25,190 --> 01:46:26,730
Good god.

1174
01:46:27,360 --> 01:46:30,440
Dear fellow, however did you manage to kill it?

1175
01:46:30,740 --> 01:46:34,190
Kill it? My oldest friend, he was.

1176
01:46:34,370 --> 01:46:38,580
- I'm so sorry, I didn't... - Don't worry yourself, you're not alone.

1177
01:46:39,080 --> 01:46:42,530
Seriously misunderstood creatures, spiders are.

1178
01:46:42,710 --> 01:46:44,920
It's the eyes, I reckon. they unnerve some folk.

1179
01:46:45,340 --> 01:46:47,290
Not to mention the pincers.

1180
01:46:51,590 --> 01:46:53,550
Yeah, I reckon that too.

1181
01:46:54,260 --> 01:46:57,630
Hagrid, the last thing I wish to be is indelicate...

1182
01:46:57,810 --> 01:47:01,890
...but acromantular venom is uncommonly rare.

1183
01:47:02,060 --> 01:47:04,270
Would you allow me to extract a vial or two?

1184
01:47:04,440 --> 01:47:07,060
Purely for academic purposes, you understand.

1185
01:47:07,230 --> 01:47:10,150
Well, I don't suppose it's going to do him much good now, is it?

1186
01:47:10,320 --> 01:47:11,520
My thoughts exactly.

1187
01:47:11,700 --> 01:47:14,820
Always have a ampoule or two about my

1188
01:47:14,820 --> 01:47:18,200
Person for just such occasions as this.

1189
01:47:18,450 --> 01:47:23,450
Old potions master's habit, you know.

1190
01:47:24,130 --> 01:47:26,580
I wish you could've seen him in his prime.

1191
01:47:26,750 --> 01:47:30,420
Magnificent, he was. Just magnificent.

1192
01:47:31,840 --> 01:47:33,420
Oh, dear.

1193
01:47:43,140 --> 01:47:46,350
- would you like me to say a few words? - yes.

1194
01:47:46,610 --> 01:47:48,150
He had a family, I trust?

1195
01:47:48,320 --> 01:47:49,810
Oh, yeah.

1196
01:47:55,160 --> 01:47:56,650
Farewell...

1197
01:47:56,820 --> 01:47:58,700
Aragog.

1198
01:48:03,210 --> 01:48:06,120
Farewell, Aragog...

1199
01:48:06,500 --> 01:48:09,170
...King of the arachnids.

1200
01:48:10,000 --> 01:48:12,580
Your body will decay...

1201
01:48:13,840 --> 01:48:16,680
...But your spirit lingers on.

1202
01:48:17,390 --> 01:48:24,010
And your human friends find solace in the loss they have sustained.

1203
01:48:39,200 --> 01:48:40,730
I had him from an egg, you know.

1204
01:48:40,730 --> 01:48:42,820
Tiny little thing he was when he hatched.

1205
01:48:43,000 --> 01:48:46,700
No bigger than a pekinese. A pekinese, mind you.

1206
01:48:46,870 --> 01:48:48,910
How sweet. I once had a fish. Francis.

1207
01:48:48,910 --> 01:48:52,040
He was very dear to me.

1208
01:48:52,210 --> 01:48:57,370
One afternoon I came downstairs, and he'd vanished.

1209
01:48:57,370 --> 01:48:58,420
Poof.

1210
01:48:59,300 --> 01:49:02,510
- That's very odd, isn't it? - it is, isn't it?

1211
01:49:02,680 --> 01:49:06,380
But that's life, I suppose.

1212
01:49:06,560 --> 01:49:11,900
You go along and then suddenly, poof!

1213
01:49:12,070 --> 01:49:15,730
- poof. - poof.

1214
01:49:30,290 --> 01:49:33,410
It was a student who gave me francis.

1215
01:49:34,420 --> 01:49:38,720
One spring afternoon I discovered a bowl on my desk...

1216
01:49:39,640 --> 01:49:42,590
...With just a few inches of clear water in it.

1217
01:49:43,390 --> 01:49:46,920
And floating on the surface was a flower petal.

1218
01:49:48,480 --> 01:49:50,930
As I watched, it sank.

1219
01:49:52,440 --> 01:49:55,280
Just before it reached the bottom...

1220
01:49:55,440 --> 01:49:56,900
...It transformed...

1221
01:49:58,280 --> 01:50:00,110
...Into a wee fish.

1222
01:50:01,780 --> 01:50:03,910
It was beautiful magic.

1223
01:50:04,910 --> 01:50:07,150
Wondrous to behold.

1224
01:50:09,790 --> 01:50:12,540
The flower petal had come from Lily.

1225
01:50:14,920 --> 01:50:15,950
Your mother.

1226
01:50:18,010 --> 01:50:20,500
The day I came downstairs...

1227
01:50:21,470 --> 01:50:23,760
...The day the bowl was empty...

1228
01:50:25,310 --> 01:50:27,460
...Was the day your mother...

1229
01:50:31,480 --> 01:50:33,470
I know why you're here.

1230
01:50:36,480 --> 01:50:38,480
But I can't help you.

1231
01:50:40,280 --> 01:50:41,990
It would ruin me.

1232
01:50:45,700 --> 01:50:48,160
Do you know why I survived, professor?

1233
01:50:48,700 --> 01:50:50,530
The night I got this?

1234
01:50:52,290 --> 01:50:53,920
Because of her.

1235
01:50:54,840 --> 01:50:56,630
Because she sacrificed herself.

1236
01:50:57,050 --> 01:50:59,420
Because she refused to step aside.

1237
01:50:59,590 --> 01:51:02,790
Because her love was more powerful than Voldemort.

1238
01:51:02,970 --> 01:51:06,670
- Don't say his name. - I'm not afraid of the name, professor.

1239
01:51:07,520 --> 01:51:09,640
I'm going to tell you something.

1240
01:51:10,560 --> 01:51:13,510
Something others have only guessed at.

1241
01:51:15,480 --> 01:51:16,980
It's true.

1242
01:51:17,570 --> 01:51:18,850
I am the chosen one.

1243
01:51:19,860 --> 01:51:22,070
Only I can destroy him, but in order to do so...

1244
01:51:22,240 --> 01:51:25,520
...I need to know what Tom Riddle

1245
01:51:25,520 --> 01:51:26,570
Asked you years ago in your office...

1246
01:51:26,740 --> 01:51:28,070
...And I need to know what you told him.

1247
01:51:28,790 --> 01:51:31,190
Be brave, professor.

1248
01:51:32,830 --> 01:51:34,910
Be brave like my mother.

1249
01:51:36,210 --> 01:51:38,880
Otherwise, you disgrace her.

1250
01:51:40,010 --> 01:51:42,290
Otherwise, she died for nothing.

1251
01:51:43,300 --> 01:51:48,510
Otherwise, the bowl will remain empty forever.

1252
01:51:59,070 --> 01:52:02,190
Please, don't think badly of me when you see it.

1253
01:52:04,200 --> 01:52:07,480
You've no idea what he was like, even then.

1254
01:52:44,240 --> 01:52:46,940
I was in the library the other night...

1255
01:52:47,110 --> 01:52:49,270
...In the restricted section...

1256
01:52:50,160 --> 01:52:53,780
...And I read something rather odd about a bit of rare magic.

1257
01:52:55,080 --> 01:52:57,830
It's called, as I understand it...

1258
01:52:59,130 --> 01:53:00,460
...A horcrux.

1259
01:53:02,300 --> 01:53:05,050
- I beg your pardon? - Horcrux.

1260
01:53:05,470 --> 01:53:08,140
I came across it when I was reading,

1261
01:53:08,300 --> 01:53:11,300
...And I didn't fully understand it.

1262
01:53:11,470 --> 01:53:13,220
I'm not sure what you were reading, Tom...

1263
01:53:13,390 --> 01:53:15,960
...But this is very dark stuff, very dark indeed.

1264
01:53:16,140 --> 01:53:17,690
Which is...

1265
01:53:18,810 --> 01:53:20,640
...Why I came to you.

1266
01:53:23,480 --> 01:53:24,940
A horcrux is an object in which

1267
01:53:24,940 --> 01:53:29,110
a person has concealed part of their soul.

1268
01:53:29,280 --> 01:53:31,900
But I don't understand how that works, sir.

1269
01:53:34,500 --> 01:53:38,490
One splits one's soul and hides part of it in an object.

1270
01:53:38,670 --> 01:53:40,010
By doing so, you're protected,

1271
01:53:40,010 --> 01:53:42,280
Should you be attacked and your body destroyed.

1272
01:53:42,460 --> 01:53:43,580
Protected?

1273
01:53:43,750 --> 01:53:46,960
That part of your soul that is hidden lives on.

1274
01:53:48,430 --> 01:53:50,830
In other words, you cannot die.

1275
01:53:58,020 --> 01:54:01,190
And how does one split his soul, sir?

1276
01:54:01,360 --> 01:54:04,140
I think you already know the answer to that, Tom.

1277
01:54:05,360 --> 01:54:06,850
Murder.

1278
01:54:07,360 --> 01:54:08,690
Yes.

1279
01:54:09,240 --> 01:54:14,150
Killing rips the soul apart. It is a violation against nature.

1280
01:54:15,040 --> 01:54:19,780
Can you only split the soul once? For instance, isn't seven...?

1281
01:54:19,960 --> 01:54:21,450
Seven?

1282
01:54:22,210 --> 01:54:27,500
Merlin's beard, Tom. Isn't it bad enough to consider killing one person?

1283
01:54:27,670 --> 01:54:31,420
To rip the soul into seven pieces...

1284
01:54:32,600 --> 01:54:35,630
This is all hypothetical, isn't it, tom? all academic?

1285
01:54:40,390 --> 01:54:41,720
Of course, sir.

1286
01:54:44,690 --> 01:54:46,680
It'll be our little secret.

1287
01:54:55,490 --> 01:54:56,740
Sir.

1288
01:55:12,130 --> 01:55:14,260
This is beyond anything I imagined.

1289
